(2558, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 17', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A hydrocolloid dressing is most appropriate for a wound that is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hydrocolloid dressings support moist wound healing and are suitable for selected wounds with minimal to moderate exudate.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2559, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 18', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is the most common type of dementia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Alzheimer\'s disease is the most common cause of dementia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2560, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 19', 'mcq', 'medium', 'All of the following are direct methods of nutritional assessment EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vital statistics are indirect indicators of population health and nutrition, unlike clinical, anthropometric, and biochemical assessments.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2561, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 20', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The hallmark clinical sign of kwashiorkor is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Oedema is the classic distinguishing clinical feature of kwashiorkor.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2562, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 21', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In the fetal skull, the suture between the two halves of the forehead bone, which usually fuses in early infancy, is the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The frontal or metopic suture separates the two halves of the frontal bone.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2563, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 22', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Folic acid supplementation before and during early pregnancy reduces the risk of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Folic acid supports neural tube development and reduces defects such as spina bifida.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2564, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 23', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The following data show the number of hours worked by 200 statistics students. What is the class width for this distribution? Number of Hours | Frequency 0 - 9 | 40 10 - 19 | 50 20 - 29 | 70 30 - 39 | 40', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The class intervals each contain 10 values, so the class width is 10.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2565, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 24', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A positive Ortolani or Barlow maneuver in a newborn suggests', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Positive Ortolani or Barlow tests suggest hip instability associated with developmental dysplasia of the hip.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2566, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 25', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A woman with polyhydramnios is at risk of which complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Excess amniotic fluid increases the risk of cord prolapse, especially following rupture of membranes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2567, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 26', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In which year were the Northern and Southern protectorates merged to form the colony and protectorate of Nigeria?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The Northern and Southern protectorates were amalgamated in 1914.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2568, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 27', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which type of study design allows researchers to infer cause and effect most strongly?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Experimental studies, especially randomized controlled trials, provide strong evidence for causal relationships.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2569, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 28', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is a life-threatening complication of severe preeclampsia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe preeclampsia can cause cerebral haemorrhage, stroke, seizures, and other life-threatening complications.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2570, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 29', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In managing shoulder dystocia, the McRoberts manoeuvre involves', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The McRoberts manoeuvre involves sharply flexing the mother\'s thighs toward her abdomen to help release the impacted shoulder.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2571, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 30', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with respiratory acidosis has CO2 retention. The underlying problem in respiratory acidosis is which physiological issue?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Inadequate alveolar ventilation causes carbon dioxide retention and lowers blood pH.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2572, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 31', 'mcq', 'medium', 'When a pregnant woman lies on her back for a long period, she might develop????????????', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The gravid uterus may compress the inferior vena cava when supine, reducing venous return and blood pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2573, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 32', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nigeria formally became a federation under the constitution of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The 1954 Constitution established Nigeria as a federation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2574, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 33', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient asks about malaria in travelers versus endemic residents. Travelers are more likely to develop severe malaria because of which factor?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Residents of endemic areas may develop partial acquired immunity after repeated exposure, whereas newcomers generally lack this protection.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2575, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 34', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Health education at primary health care level is most effective when it', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Community involvement improves relevance, understanding, participation, and adoption of healthy practices.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2576, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 35', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A newborn develops tremors and irritability after birth from a diabetic mother. This is commonly due to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Infants of diabetic mothers are at risk of hypoglycaemia after birth because maternal glucose supply stops while elevated fetal insulin may persist.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2577, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 36', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Electroencephalography is mainly used to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'EEG records the brain\'s electrical activity and helps identify abnormalities such as seizures.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2578, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 37', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which is a danger sign in pregnancy requiring immediate care?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vaginal bleeding during pregnancy may indicate a serious complication and requires prompt assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2579, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 38', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which nursing activity best describes health promotion?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Health promotion involves helping people adopt behaviours that improve and maintain health.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2580, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 39', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In email, BCC is used to:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'BCC hides the addresses of blind-copied recipients from other email recipients.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2581, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 40', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A key sign of uterine rupture during labour is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Uterine rupture may cause sudden, severe abdominal pain and requires emergency obstetric management.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2582, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 41', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Furosemide acts mainly on the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Furosemide is a loop diuretic that inhibits sodium and chloride reabsorption in the thick ascending limb of the loop of Henle.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2583, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 42', 'mcq', 'medium', 'For a patient with hepatic encephalopathy, the most appropriate general dietary plan is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Patients generally need adequate energy and protein; protein restriction is not routinely recommended and should be individualized when necessary.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2584, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 43', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Colloid osmotic pressure is the osmotic pressure exerted mainly by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Plasma proteins, especially albumin, create colloid osmotic pressure that helps retain fluid within blood vessels.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2585, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 44', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is caring for a client with active, laryngeal tuberculosis in the hospital. The most appropriate type of isolation precaution is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Active laryngeal tuberculosis spreads through airborne particles, so airborne precautions are required.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2586, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 45', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In supine hypotensive syndrome, the gravid uterus compresses the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Compression of the inferior vena cava reduces venous return to the heart and can cause maternal hypotension.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2587, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 46', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client with unexplained vaginal bleeding should defer which method until evaluated', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Unexplained vaginal bleeding should be evaluated before IUCD insertion to exclude serious underlying causes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2588, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 47', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A fracture at the base of the first metacarpal affecting thumb movement is BEST described as', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A Bennett fracture involves the base of the first metacarpal and may affect thumb joint stability.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2589, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 48', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is a function of the respiratory system?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The respiratory system exchanges oxygen and carbon dioxide between the air and blood.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2590, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 49', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Colour vision is mediated by which retinal cells?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cone photoreceptors detect colour and function best in bright light.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2591, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 50', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which form of written communication always carries a subject line?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Memos commonly include a subject line that identifies the purpose of the communication.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2592, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 51', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A woman in labour with breech presentation is at risk of which complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Breech presentation increases the risk of umbilical cord prolapse, which can compromise fetal oxygen supply.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2593, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 52', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which evaluation type measures long-term program impact?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Summative evaluation assesses overall results and outcomes, often including the impact of a completed programme.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2594, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 53', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient on thiazide diuretic develops hyponatremia. Thiazides impair dilution by blocking sodium reabsorption in which nephron segment?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thiazide diuretics inhibit sodium chloride reabsorption in the distal convoluted tubule, increasing the risk of hyponatraemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2595, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 54', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which capacity does community resilience primarily describe?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Community resilience is the ability of a community to withstand, adapt to, and recover from adversity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2596, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 55', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The rationale for advising a constipated pregnant client to increase fluid intake is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Adequate fluid intake helps soften stool and makes bowel movements easier.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2597, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 56', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which diuretic can cause ototoxicity if given too fast IV?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rapid intravenous administration of furosemide increases the risk of hearing damage.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2598, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 57', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which pathway do inhaled corticosteroids primarily prevent exacerbations through?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Inhaled corticosteroids reduce airway inflammation, helping prevent asthma exacerbations.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2599, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 58', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client with a newly applied plaster cast on their leg complains of intense pain unrelieved by analgesics. The nurse\'s priority action is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe pain unrelieved by analgesics may indicate neurovascular compromise or compartment syndrome and requires immediate assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2600, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 59', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of these cardiovascular changes occur in pregnancy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Plasma volume increases more than red blood cell mass during pregnancy, producing physiological haemodilution.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2601, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 60', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Peptic ulcer disease most commonly affects the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Peptic ulcers most commonly occur in the stomach or duodenum.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2602, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 61', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A woman with severe pre-eclampsia develops right upper quadrant pain. This most likely indicates', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Right upper quadrant or epigastric pain may indicate liver involvement and possible HELLP syndrome.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2603, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 62', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Calcium channel blockers relieve angina mainly by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Calcium channel blockers reduce vascular resistance and may improve coronary blood flow, lowering myocardial oxygen demand.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2604, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 63', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The part of the sclera perforated for passage of optic nerve fibres is the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The lamina cribrosa is the perforated part of the sclera through which optic nerve fibres pass.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2605, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 64', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The primary goal of medical treatment for endometriosis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Medical treatment mainly aims to control pain and symptoms; it does not reliably cure endometriosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2606, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 65', 'mcq', 'medium', 'An early symptom of strangulation in bilateral inguinal hernia is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Strangulation compromises blood supply to the herniated tissue and can cause severe abdominal or groin pain.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2607, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 66', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A mother brings her infant with severe diarrhoea to the clinic. The nurse notes the infant has sunken fontanelles, tachycardia, and is unable to drink. The priority nursing action is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe dehydration with inability to drink requires urgent facility-based rehydration, usually with intravenous fluids according to protocol.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2608, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 67', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A woman at 14 weeks\' gestation has no documented tetanus-containing vaccine doses and needs catch-up Td vaccination. What is the appropriate response?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tetanus-containing vaccination can be given during pregnancy when indicated; the schedule depends on previous documented doses and local guidance.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2609, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 68', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A mother worries that her breast milk looks thin and watery at the start of a feed. The midwife should explain that this milk is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Foremilk is the milk available at the beginning of a feed and is often thinner in appearance.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2610, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 69', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client with acute decompensated heart failure is receiving an IV infusion of dobutamine. The nurse expects this medication to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dobutamine is an inotropic medication that increases myocardial contractility and can improve cardiac output.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2611, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 70', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Emotional intelligence is the ability to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Emotional intelligence involves recognising, understanding, and managing one\'s emotions and those of others.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2612, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 71', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient taking acetaminophen exceeds the maximum daily dose. The major toxicity concern with acetaminophen overdose is which organ damage?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Acetaminophen overdose can cause severe liver injury due to the accumulation of a toxic metabolite.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2613, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 72', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The internal pudendal artery arises directly from which parent vessel?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The internal pudendal artery usually arises from the anterior division of the internal iliac artery.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2614, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 73', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The ascending colon is supplied mainly by branches of the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The superior mesenteric artery supplies most of the ascending colon through branches including the ileocolic and right colic arteries.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2615, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 74', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Penicillins and cephalosporins, which are considered safe in pregnancy, act by inhibiting bacterial', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Beta-lactam antibiotics inhibit bacterial cell wall synthesis, leading to bacterial death.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2616, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 75', 'mcq', 'medium', 'At primary health care level, oral rehydration solution is primarily used to treat', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Oral rehydration solution replaces water and electrolytes lost through diarrhoea.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2617, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 76', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Orange discoloration of urine and tears is a harmless side effect of which anti-TB drug?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rifampicin commonly causes orange-red discoloration of urine, sweat, saliva, and tears.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2618, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 77', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The ethical principle of truth telling is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Veracity is the ethical duty to tell the truth and provide accurate information.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2619, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 78', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The normal respiratory rate for an adult at rest is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The normal resting respiratory rate for a healthy adult is generally 12?20 breaths per minute.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2620, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 79', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Disappearance of the Moro and rooting reflexes at the expected age indicates', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Primitive reflexes normally disappear as the central nervous system matures and voluntary control develops.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2621, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 80', 'mcq', 'medium', '0.25 L equals', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'One litre equals 1,000 mL; therefore, 0.25 L equals 250 mL.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2622, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 81', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The intertragal notch of the pinna lies between the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The intertragal notch is the depression between the tragus and antitragus of the external ear.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2623, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 82', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A vague feeling of discomfort or dread whose source is unknown is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Anxiety is a feeling of apprehension or uneasiness when the source of threat may be unclear.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2624, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 83', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is a primary (first-line) defence against infection?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Intact skin forms a physical barrier that prevents pathogens from entering the body.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2625, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 84', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The narrow fibrous joints between the bones of the fetal skull are called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sutures are fibrous joints between the bones of the fetal skull; fontanelles are the wider membranous spaces between them.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2626, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 85', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Drug resistance in tuberculosis management is due to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Genetic mutations in Mycobacterium tuberculosis can produce resistance to anti-tuberculosis drugs.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
