(2694, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 153', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The usual initial hydrocortisone dose for an adult in adrenal crisis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The usual initial adult dose for adrenal crisis is 100 mg hydrocortisone intravenously or intramuscularly, followed by ongoing treatment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2695, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 154', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which is the most common cause of maternal mortality worldwide?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Postpartum haemorrhage is a leading direct cause of maternal death worldwide.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2696, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 155', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A non-immune traveler develops severe malaria. Non-immune individuals are at higher risk for severe disease due to lack of which protection?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'People without acquired immunity to malaria are at greater risk of severe disease when infected.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2697, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 156', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which step involves primary nursing intervention for impaired gas exchange?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Supplemental oxygen can improve oxygenation when indicated, alongside assessment and treatment of the underlying cause.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2698, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 157', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with hypocalcaemia develops tetany. IV calcium gluconate is given primarily to relieve', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Intravenous calcium gluconate raises serum calcium and helps relieve neuromuscular irritability, including tetany and carpopedal spasm.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2699, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 158', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Transfer of antibodies from the mother to the fetus across the placenta is termed', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Maternal IgG antibodies cross the placenta and provide natural passive immunity to the fetus.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2700, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 159', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Eating behavior is controlled by the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The hypothalamus helps regulate hunger, satiety, and feeding behaviour.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2701, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 160', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the primary benefit of delayed cord clamping?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Delayed cord clamping allows additional placental blood to reach the newborn, improving haemoglobin levels and iron stores.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2702, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 161', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse would advise the mother of an eight-month-old to stimulate cognitive development by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Peek-a-boo encourages attention, memory, object permanence, and social interaction in infants.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2703, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 162', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The continuation phase of standard TB treatment typically involves the administration of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The standard continuation phase for drug-susceptible TB commonly uses isoniazid and rifampicin to eliminate remaining bacteria.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2704, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 163', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A key nursing diagnosis for a client during a sickle cell vaso-occlusive crisis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sickled red blood cells obstruct small blood vessels, reducing tissue perfusion and causing severe pain.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2705, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 164', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In Caplan\'s model, phase II in the development of a crisis is characterised by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Phase II involves increased tension after a stressful event and initial attempts to use usual coping mechanisms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2706, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 165', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The TNM staging system: \"T\" stands for', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'T describes the primary tumour\'s size and extent of local invasion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2707, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 166', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Recurrent infections, chronic conjunctivitis, and chronic diarrhea indicate a possible attack on the ???.', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Recurrent infections and persistent diarrhoea may indicate impaired immune function.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2708, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 167', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A long-term goal for a client with a new colostomy would be', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Demonstrating correct pouch care by discharge is a longer-term self-management goal.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2709, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 168', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The primary symptom of generalised anxiety disorder is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Generalised anxiety disorder involves excessive, difficult-to-control worry about multiple areas of life.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2710, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 169', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is NOT a main focus of the Integrated Management of Childhood Illness strategy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'IMCI primarily addresses common childhood illnesses and danger signs rather than congenital heart defects.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2711, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 170', 'mcq', 'medium', 'According to Piaget, preschool children are in the stage of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Piaget\'s preoperational stage typically covers ages two to seven years.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2712, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 171', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which imbalance does citrate toxicity during massive transfusion primarily cause?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Citrate used in stored blood products binds calcium, potentially causing hypocalcaemia during massive transfusion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2713, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 172', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse is teaching about carcinogens to a community health group. Which of the following substances is NOT classified as a carcinogen?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vitamin C is not classified as a carcinogen; tobacco smoke, ultraviolet radiation, and asbestos are established carcinogenic exposures.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2714, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 173', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Analgesics are used to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Analgesics are medicines used to reduce or relieve pain.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2715, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 174', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The gallbladder in pregnancy is prone to delayed emptying and cholestasis, which increases the risk of developing what', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pregnancy-related hormonal changes slow gallbladder emptying and increase bile cholesterol saturation, raising gallstone risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2716, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 175', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Materials gotten from the physical remains of man\'s past activities are studied through', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Archaeology studies past human activities through material remains and artefacts.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2717, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 176', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In IMCI fever assessment, ?general danger sign + fever? indicates', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A general danger sign with fever requires urgent assessment and classification as possible severe disease.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2718, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 177', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The term ?schizophrenia? was coined by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Eugen Bleuler introduced the term schizophrenia in the early twentieth century.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2719, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 178', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Crisis intervention is primarily focused on', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Crisis intervention prioritises immediate safety, stabilisation, and restoration of coping.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2720, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 179', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Most part of heat-loss from the body occurs through the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The skin is the main route of heat loss through radiation, conduction, convection, and evaporation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2721, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 180', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A research study undertaken to solve an immediate practical problem, with the goal of adding to scientific knowledge is research', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Applied research investigates practical problems and aims to produce findings that can be used in real-world settings.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2722, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 181', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Generalised anxiety disorder is characterised by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Persistent excessive worry across several areas of life is the hallmark of generalised anxiety disorder.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2723, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 182', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with HIV/TB co-infection requires treatment for both conditions. Rifampicin interacts with many ARVs by inducing which enzyme?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rifampicin strongly induces CYP3A4 and other drug-metabolising pathways, which can reduce concentrations of several antiretroviral medicines.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2724, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 183', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What type of immunity is conferred by vaccination?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vaccination stimulates the person\'s own immune system to produce a protective response, giving artificial active immunity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2725, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 184', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How many pairs of spinal nerves are found in humans?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Humans have 31 pairs of spinal nerves.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2726, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 185', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The hormone prolactin, which increases significantly during pregnancy, has what primary role', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Prolactin promotes breast development and prepares the mammary glands for milk production.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2727, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 186', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which nursing diagnosis is priority for patient with severe burns in first 24 hours?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Major burns cause fluid shifts and capillary leakage, placing the patient at high risk of hypovolaemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2728, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 187', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The process of involving people and giving them responsibility in a PHC programme is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Community participation involves people in planning, implementing, and taking responsibility for health programmes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2729, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 188', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client asks why their spleen might be enlarged during typhoid fever. The nurse explains it is due to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Typhoid infection can stimulate the reticuloendothelial system, including macrophage activity, contributing to splenic enlargement.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2730, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 189', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client with a subdural haematoma is typically characterized by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A subdural haematoma commonly results from torn bridging veins and may cause symptoms that develop gradually.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2731, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 190', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Compared with a manager, an entrepreneur is mainly characterised by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Entrepreneurs identify opportunities and establish new ventures, often involving innovation and calculated risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2732, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 191', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Exchange of oxygen and nutrients between mother and fetus takes place in the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The placenta enables the exchange of oxygen, nutrients, and waste products between maternal and fetal circulation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2733, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 192', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The highest risk of TB transmission to family occurs through', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tuberculosis spreads through infectious airborne particles, especially in poorly ventilated indoor spaces.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2734, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 193', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of these is a main muscle involved in respiration?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The diaphragm is the primary muscle of inspiration, contracting to expand the thoracic cavity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2735, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 194', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Among these IV fluids, the isotonic crystalloid is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lactated Ringer solution is an isotonic crystalloid used to replace fluids and electrolytes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2736, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 195', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The successful transition through the fourth stage is best indicated by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A firm uterus and stable vital signs indicate effective uterine contraction and maternal stability after delivery.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2737, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 196', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following instruments can be used to visualize the retina when assessing a patient eye?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'An ophthalmoscope is used to examine the retina and other structures at the back of the eye.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2738, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 197', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The feature that distinguishes periodontitis from gingivitis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Periodontitis involves destruction of the supporting tissues of the teeth, including alveolar bone loss.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2739, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 198', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is an environmental stressor?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Extreme cold is an environmental stressor because it originates from the physical surroundings.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2740, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 199', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Pain is best described as', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pain is subjective because it is experienced and reported differently by each individual.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2741, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 200', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which is the most common cause of polyhydramnios?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Many cases of polyhydramnios have no identifiable cause and are classified as idiopathic.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2742, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 201', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The equipment and programs used to process raw data into information are called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Information technology includes computer hardware, software, and systems used to process and manage information.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2743, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 202', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Before the eruption of the wisdom teeth, an adult has how many teeth', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'An adult normally has 28 teeth before the four third molars, or wisdom teeth, erupt.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2744, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 203', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A FHR pattern showing a gradual decrease that mirrors the contraction is identified as an early deceleration, which is caused by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Early decelerations usually result from fetal head compression during uterine contractions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2745, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 204', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following classes of drugs produces the same effect on the pupil as a bright light?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Miotics constrict the pupil, similar to the pupillary response to bright light.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2746, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 205', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The reproductive health package that addresses maternal, newborn, and family planning services in emergencies is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The Minimum Initial Service Package (MISP) provides essential reproductive health services during emergencies.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2747, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 206', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client with maxillary sinusitis will complain of pain', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The maxillary sinuses lie in the cheek area, so inflammation commonly causes cheek pain or pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2748, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 207', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which is a barrier to communication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Medical jargon may be difficult for patients to understand and can interfere with effective communication.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2749, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 208', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The primary role of surfactant in the lungs is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pulmonary surfactant reduces alveolar surface tension and helps prevent alveolar collapse.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2750, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 209', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A clay-coloured stool is an indication of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Clay-coloured stool may occur when bile cannot reach the intestine because of biliary obstruction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2751, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 210', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with MRSA infection requires antibiotic therapy. Which antibiotic is the drug of choice for MRSA?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vancomycin is commonly used for serious MRSA infections, depending on the infection site and susceptibility results.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2752, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 211', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A woman at 28 weeks presents with a sudden gush of clear fluid without contractions. The most likely diagnosis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A sudden gush of fluid before 37 weeks and before labour suggests preterm prelabour rupture of membranes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2753, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 212', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which is a sign of hypoglycemia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hypoglycemia can cause sweating, tremors, and confusion due to inadequate glucose availability.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2754, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 213', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Blood group antigens are found mainly on the surface of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'ABO and Rh blood group antigens are primarily located on red blood cell membranes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2755, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 214', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A child with pertussis (whooping cough) is in the paroxysmal stage. The priority nursing intervention during a coughing spell is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Upright positioning and airway monitoring help maintain breathing and identify respiratory distress during coughing spells.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2756, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 215', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The application of economic theory and concepts in health care is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Health economics applies economic principles to healthcare resources, services, costs, and outcomes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2757, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 216', 'mcq', 'medium', '??.. is gradual in onset and last a relatively long time', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chronic illness generally develops gradually and persists for a long period.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2758, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 217', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The process of sperm cell formation in the testes is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Spermatogenesis is the process by which sperm cells develop in the seminiferous tubules of the testes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2759, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 218', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Part of the management of an exceptional child is that the child should', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Education suited to the child\'s abilities and needs promotes development, inclusion, and independence.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
(2760, 9, 31, NULL, 'AC.DAY 219', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Episiotomy during a normal vaginal delivery should be performed', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Routine episiotomy is not recommended; it should be performed when clinically indicated.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 14:34:05', '2026-10-10 14:34:05', NULL),
