(2826, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-29', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A debilitated patient with acute tracheobronchitis is at higher risk for which life-threatening complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Debilitated patients have less respiratory reserve and are at increased risk of severe infection progressing to respiratory failure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2827, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-30', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which underlying condition is most commonly associated with the development of a transudative pleural effusion?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Heart failure increases hydrostatic pressure and is the most common cause of transudative pleural effusion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2828, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-31', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient has been receiving high-dose oral Prednisolone for three weeks for a severe asthma exacerbation. The provider decides to discontinue the therapy. What is the critical physiological rationale for gradually tapering the dose rather than stopping abruptly?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Systemic corticosteroids can suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis; tapering allows endogenous cortisol production to recover and reduces the risk of adrenal insufficiency.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2829, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-32', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient who discontinued Bedaquiline therapy two months ago is admitted for an unrelated procedure. The nurse notes the physician is still cautious about prescribing QTc-prolonging drugs. Why?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bedaquiline has a very long terminal half-life, so drug exposure and QT-prolonging effects can persist after treatment ends.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2830, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-33', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is suspected of having a pleural effusion. Which specific x-ray position is best for visualizing \'layering out\' of the fluid?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lateral decubitus positioning allows free pleural fluid to layer along the dependent chest wall, making small effusions easier to detect.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2831, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-34', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nursing assessment for bronchospasm in a patient with COPD includes which of the following?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bronchospasm causes airway narrowing, decreased airflow, wheezing, and impaired gas exchange.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2832, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-35', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient presents to a community clinic with a low-grade fever, chills, and sneezing. Based on the notes, what is the expected duration of these symptoms for a typical case of viral rhinitis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Typical viral rhinitis symptoms generally improve within several days, commonly about 3?5 days, although some symptoms may last longer.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2833, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-36', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Acute pharyngitis of a bacterial nature is most commonly caused by:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Group A beta-hemolytic Streptococcus (Streptococcus pyogenes) is the most common bacterial cause of acute pharyngitis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2834, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-37', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which statement best describes the primary reason why adequate treatment of an upper respiratory tract infection (URI) is essential in preventing acute tracheobronchitis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Respiratory viral infections can impair local defenses and increase susceptibility to secondary bacterial infection of the lower respiratory tract.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2835, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-38', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the underlying clinical reasoning for the \'1-week rule\' regarding expectorant use?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Persistent cough despite about a week of self-treatment may indicate an underlying condition requiring medical assessment rather than continued symptomatic treatment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2836, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-39', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What term is applied to the volume of air that moves into the lungs while breathing at rest?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tidal volume is the amount of air inhaled or exhaled during a normal quiet breath.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2837, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-40', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A gastric pH of 3.0 indicates the tube is likely in which location?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Gastric aspirate is normally acidic; a pH of 3.0 is consistent with placement in the stomach.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2838, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-41', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which physiologic change characterizes the airflow limitation found in COPD?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'COPD airflow limitation is progressive and results from chronic abnormal inflammatory responses and structural changes in the airways and lung parenchyma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2839, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-42', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A laboratory report indicates a patient\'s Mycobacterium tuberculosis isolate is resistant to both Isoniazid and Rifampicin. Based on this, how should the nurse classify the patient\'s disease?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Resistance to at least isoniazid and rifampicin defines multidrug-resistant tuberculosis (MDR-TB).', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2840, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-43', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following can be used to calculate the residual volume of the lungs?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Residual volume equals total lung capacity minus vital capacity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2841, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-44', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is preparing to administer Xylometazoline to a 5-year-old pediatric patient in the ward. Which concentration and dosage frequency must the nurse verify as safe and appropriate for this specific age group?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The source-intended pediatric regimen is 0.05% xylometazoline given as 2?3 drops every 8?12 hours. Pediatric concentrations and dosing should be verified against the local product labeling.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2842, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-45', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient who underwent a supraglottic laryngectomy is beginning oral intake. The nurse should prioritize teaching the patient which technique?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The supraglottic swallow technique helps protect the airway during swallowing after supraglottic laryngectomy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2843, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-46', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which chemical mediators released by mast cells are responsible for the inflammatory response in asthma?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Mast-cell mediators including histamine and leukotrienes contribute to bronchoconstriction and airway inflammation in asthma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2844, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-47', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is considered a primary pharmacological limitation of second-generation antihistamines compared to first-generation agents?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Second-generation antihistamines cause less CNS and anticholinergic effects but generally have less antiemetic, antitussive, and sedative activity than first-generation agents.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2845, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-48', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Severing the nerves that innervate the breathing muscles may lead rapidly to death. Will a spinal cord break between C6 and C7 leave the victim able to breathe?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The phrenic nerves arise mainly from C3?C5 and innervate the diaphragm, so a lesion below C5 may preserve basic diaphragmatic breathing, although accessory muscle function can be impaired.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2846, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-49', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The primary presenting symptom observed in patients with emphysema is:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dyspnea, particularly progressive exertional dyspnea, is a prominent presenting symptom of emphysema.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2847, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-50', 'mcq', 'medium', 'One of the following statements is correct. Which one?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Normally, negative intrapleural pressure is maintained within the pleural space between the visceral and parietal pleura.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2848, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-51', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What happens when carbon dioxide levels in the blood increase?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Increased carbon dioxide combines with water to form carbonic acid, increasing hydrogen ions and lowering blood pH.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2849, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-52', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During a pharmacology review, a nurse compares Tiotropium Bromide with Ipratropium Bromide. Which statement accurately highlights the primary clinical difference between these two anticholinergics?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tiotropium is a long-acting inhaled antimuscarinic generally given once daily, while ipratropium is shorter acting and usually requires multiple daily doses.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2850, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-53', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is teaching a patient about the duration of oral antibiotic therapy for a lung abscess. Which timeframe is correct?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lung abscesses usually require prolonged antibiotic treatment, often several weeks, depending on clinical and radiologic response.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2851, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-54', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with chronic bronchitis asks why they are prescribed Carbocysteine instead of a strong cough suppressant. What is the nurse\'s best physiological explanation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Carbocysteine is a mucolytic that helps reduce mucus viscosity, allowing secretions to be cleared more effectively; suppressing a productive cough may hinder clearance.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2852, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-55', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How do leukotriene modifiers (inhibitors) assist in asthma management?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Leukotriene receptor antagonists block leukotriene-mediated effects such as bronchoconstriction, mucus production, and airway inflammation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2853, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-56', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with pneumonia is placed in a semi-Fowler\'s position. What is the primary rationale for this nursing intervention?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Semi-Fowler\'s positioning improves lung expansion, eases breathing, and can facilitate secretion clearance.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2854, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-57', 'mcq', 'medium', 'When should a COPD patient use a bronchodilator prophylactically?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A prescribed short-acting bronchodilator may be used before activities that commonly trigger exertional breathlessness, such as walking.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2855, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-58', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the function of ciliated cells in the lungs?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ciliated epithelial cells move mucus and trapped particles toward the pharynx through the mucociliary escalator.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2856, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-59', 'mcq', 'medium', 'To what does external respiration refer?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'External respiration is the exchange of oxygen and carbon dioxide between alveolar air and pulmonary capillary blood.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2857, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-60', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with cystic fibrosis is prescribed Dornase alfa. How should the nurse explain the unique mechanism of this specific drug compared to other mucolytics?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dornase alfa is recombinant human DNase that cleaves extracellular DNA in thick cystic-fibrosis mucus, reducing its viscosity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2858, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-61', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A Mantoux skin test is considered not significant if the size of the induration is:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'An induration of less than 5 mm is generally considered negative or not significant for most individuals.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2859, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-62', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How long is the typical exposure period required before the onset of symptoms like shortness of breath in silicosis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chronic silicosis usually develops after prolonged occupational exposure to silica dust, often over 10 to 20 years.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2860, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-63', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A bronchiole differs from tertiary (and smaller) bronchi in that it:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bronchioles lack cartilage but contain prominent smooth muscle in their walls.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2861, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-64', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Streptococcus pneumoniae is the most common organism responsible for which type of pneumonia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Streptococcus pneumoniae is a leading bacterial cause of community-acquired pneumonia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2862, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-65', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Neuromuscular blockers are given to patients on ventilators in ARF for the following reasons EXCEPT:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Neuromuscular blockers may improve ventilator synchrony but do not directly increase the patient\'s respiratory rate.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2863, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-66', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse is assessing a patient at risk for lung abscess. Which condition most significantly increases the risk of developing this complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Impaired consciousness and a weak cough reflex increase aspiration risk, which is a major risk factor for lung abscess.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2864, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-67', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A pregnant patient is successfully started on a safe first-line ATT regimen. To prevent neurological complications for both the mother and fetus, which supplement is mandatory?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pyridoxine (vitamin B6) is given with isoniazid during pregnancy to reduce the risk of peripheral neuropathy and deficiency.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2865, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-68', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which genetic factor predisposes young, non-smoking patients to develop lobular emphysema?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency causes inadequate protection against proteolytic enzymes and can lead to early-onset emphysema, especially in nonsmokers.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2866, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-69', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which buffer system of the body is affected by the action of the lungs?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The lungs regulate carbon dioxide, which directly affects the carbonic acid-bicarbonate buffer system and blood pH.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2867, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-70', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The \'triple response\' of histamine consists of which three clinical signs?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The histamine triple response consists of a red flare, a wheal, and itching at the site of histamine release.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2868, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-71', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which diagnostic criterion is used to differentiate ARDS from cardiogenic pulmonary edema?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'ARDS is noncardiogenic pulmonary edema; absence of evidence of left atrial hypertension or cardiac failure helps distinguish it from cardiogenic edema.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2869, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-72', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient presents with dyspnea, tachycardia, and central cyanosis. Which assessment finding is most characteristic of acute lobar atelectasis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Atelectasis can cause hypoxemia and respiratory distress, with worsening dyspnea when supine and associated anxiety.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2870, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-73', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with chronic sinusitis has failed 4 weeks of medical therapy. What surgical intervention is usually indicated?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Endoscopic sinus surgery can restore sinus drainage and ventilation when chronic sinusitis persists despite appropriate medical therapy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2871, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-74', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nursing student is reviewing the pathophysiology of rhinitis. The student correctly identifies that the condition involves the inflammation and irritation of which specific anatomical structures?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rhinitis is inflammation and irritation of the nasal mucous membranes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2872, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-75', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a lung abscess develops sudden, massive hemoptysis. Which medical intervention should the nurse anticipate?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Massive hemoptysis requires urgent airway assessment and control of bleeding; bronchoscopy can help localize and manage the bleeding source.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2873, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-76', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient in acute respiratory distress is mistakenly administered an inhalational corticosteroid instead of a short-acting beta2 agonist. Why is this choice of medication ineffective in an acute crisis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Inhaled corticosteroids reduce airway inflammation but do not provide rapid direct bronchodilation; short-acting beta2 agonists provide rapid relief during acute bronchospasm.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2874, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-77', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Patients with musculoskeletal or neurologic disorders are at risk for atelectasis primarily due to:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Neuromuscular weakness can reduce lung expansion and impair effective coughing, promoting secretion retention and atelectasis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2875, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-78', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the primary purpose of a Greenfield filter?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A Greenfield inferior vena cava filter traps emboli from the lower venous circulation and helps prevent them from reaching the pulmonary arteries.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2876, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-79', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which type of lung cancer is most prevalent in both men and women and often presents as peripheral nodules?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Adenocarcinoma is the most common lung cancer type and commonly arises in peripheral lung tissue.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2877, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-80', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The most common bacterial pathogen associated with tonsillitis and adenoiditis is:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Group A beta-hemolytic Streptococcus, particularly Streptococcus pyogenes, is a common bacterial cause of tonsillitis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2878, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-81', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the precise mechanism by which Omalizumab reduces the frequency of asthma exacerbations in patients with severe allergic asthma?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Omalizumab is an anti-IgE monoclonal antibody that binds free IgE and reduces IgE-mediated allergic inflammation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2879, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-82', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which surgical procedure involves the removal of an entire lung?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A pneumonectomy is the surgical removal of an entire lung.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2880, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-83', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why might a patient with Cor Pulmonale experience headache and somnolence?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chronic hypoventilation associated with severe lung disease can cause hypercapnia, producing headache and somnolence.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2881, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-84', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is instructed to use Flunisolide nasal spray every 12 hours for chronic sinusitis. After three weeks of consistent, correct use, the patient reports zero improvement in their congestion. What is the standard clinical protocol regarding pharmacokinetics in this scenario?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'If there is no clinical benefit after an adequate trial, the treatment should be reassessed rather than increasing the dose or frequency without medical review.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2882, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-85', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is suspected of having a PE. Which diagnostic test is the test of choice to rule out clinically important PE?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'In patients with low or intermediate clinical probability, a negative D-dimer can effectively rule out clinically significant PE; imaging is reserved for patients who require further evaluation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2883, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-86', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Rhinoviruses are frequent causes of:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rhinoviruses are among the most common causes of the common cold.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2884, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-87', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following describes the fundamental goal of the continuation phase in a Category II TB treatment regimen?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The continuation phase aims to eliminate remaining susceptible and persistent bacilli and reduce the risk of relapse after the intensive phase.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2885, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-88', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In asbestosis, what happens to the pleura as the disease progresses?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Asbestos exposure can cause pleural thickening and characteristic pleural plaques.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2886, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-89', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How many pairs of nares (nostrils) are found in the upper respiratory tract?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Humans have one pair of external nares, consisting of two nostrils.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2887, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-90', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with primary pulmonary hypertension is most likely to belong to which demographic group?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Primary pulmonary arterial hypertension has historically been more common in women, particularly younger and middle-aged women.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2888, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-91', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which is the most frequent sign associated with a possible pulmonary embolism?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tachypnea is one of the most common clinical signs of pulmonary embolism and reflects impaired oxygenation and increased respiratory drive.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2889, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-92', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse is teaching a patient how to use Beclomethasone Dipropionate Rotacaps. Which action by the patient indicates a need for further instruction?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rotacaps are intended for inhalation through a Rotahaler and should never be swallowed. Swallowing the capsule indicates incorrect use.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2890, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-93', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient receiving treatment for multidrug-resistant TB is prescribed Cycloserine. The nurse should carefully screen the patient\'s history for which condition?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cycloserine can cause serious neuropsychiatric effects and seizures, so patients with a history of seizures or severe mental illness require careful assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2891, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-94', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient taking oral Diphenhydramine 50 mg for severe pruritus is monitored on the telemetry unit. What direct cardiovascular effects should the nurse anticipate observing following this oral dose?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Diphenhydramine can produce QT prolongation, particularly at higher doses or in susceptible patients, increasing the risk of cardiac arrhythmias.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2892, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-95', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a history of cardiac arrhythmias requires a daily antihistamine for atopic eczema. Which second-generation antihistamine is specifically noted as being safe for cardiac patients?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Fexofenadine is a second-generation antihistamine with minimal cardiac effects and is generally considered a safer option in patients at risk of arrhythmias.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2893, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-96', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which patient is at the highest risk for developing a lung abscess based on pathophysiology?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dysphagia increases the risk of aspiration of oral or gastric contents, which can introduce anaerobic bacteria into the lungs and lead to a lung abscess.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2894, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-97', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) asks the provider for a prescription for Montelukast, stating their friend with asthma takes it with great results. The nurse understands this request will likely be denied because:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Montelukast blocks cysteinyl leukotriene receptors and is primarily useful in asthma. Leukotriene pathways are not the main therapeutic target in COPD.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2895, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-98', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In which form is the majority of CO? transported in the blood?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Approximately 70% of carbon dioxide is transported in the blood as bicarbonate ions after conversion within red blood cells.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2896, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-99', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why might a patient with a prolonged tracheostomy be at higher risk for aspiration?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Prolonged tracheostomy can impair laryngeal elevation and reduce protective laryngeal and glottic reflexes, increasing aspiration risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2897, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-100', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which clinical sign is considered a late indicator of hypoxemia in a patient with severe lobar atelectasis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Central cyanosis is a late sign of significant hypoxemia. Tachycardia and other compensatory changes generally occur earlier.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2898, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-101', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Following systemic absorption and hepatic metabolism, what is the primary physiological route of excretion for an oral decongestant like Pseudoephedrine?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pseudoephedrine and its metabolites are primarily eliminated through the kidneys, making renal excretion the main route of elimination.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2899, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-102', 'mcq', 'medium', 'When evaluating a patient for antitussive therapy, why is it critical to assess the \'duration\' of the cough?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The duration helps distinguish an acute cough from a chronic cough. Persistent cough may indicate an underlying disorder that requires evaluation rather than prolonged suppression.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2900, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-103', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is evaluating an HIV-positive patient for latent TB. The patient has a recent Mantoux conversion but a clear chest X-ray and no symptoms. What is the most appropriate prophylactic intervention?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A positive Mantoux conversion without evidence of active TB indicates latent infection. Isoniazid preventive therapy has historically been used to reduce progression to active TB; current regimens may vary according to guidelines.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2901, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-104', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In a healthy person, which of these lung volumes should be the largest?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vital capacity is the largest of the listed individual lung volumes and represents the maximum amount of air exhaled after maximal inspiration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2902, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-105', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient receiving a nebulized treatment of Salbutamol and Ipratropium bromide complains of sudden, severe eye pain and blurred vision. What is the most likely cause?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ipratropium is an anticholinergic drug. If nebulized mist enters the eyes, it can precipitate acute angle-closure glaucoma, especially in susceptible patients.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2903, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-106', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is prescribed Potassium Iodide for chronic bronchitis. Which assessment finding should the nurse prioritize to prevent a dangerous complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Excessive iodide exposure can cause iodism, characterized by metallic taste, excessive salivation, skin eruptions, and other toxicity symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2904, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-107', 'mcq', 'medium', 'To which of the following does the term \'respiration\' NOT apply?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Respiration includes external gas exchange, internal gas exchange, and cellular respiration. Conversion of carbon dioxide to bicarbonate is a transport mechanism rather than a separate type of respiration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2905, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-108', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which assessment finding in a patient with CF indicates chronic hypoxemia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Clubbing of the fingers and toes is associated with chronic hypoxemia and long-standing pulmonary disease, including cystic fibrosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2906, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-109', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What mechanism transports the largest portion of oxygen around the body?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Most oxygen in the blood is transported bound to haemoglobin within red blood cells, while only a small amount is dissolved in plasma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2907, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-110', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with rib fractures is breathing shallowly and avoiding coughing. What is the most significant risk of this behavior?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pain-induced shallow breathing and avoidance of coughing reduce ventilation and secretion clearance, increasing the risk of atelectasis and hypoxemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2908, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-111', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the primary purpose of using \'flutter devices\' or PEP masks in cystic fibrosis care?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Flutter devices and PEP masks create positive expiratory pressure that helps mobilize and clear thick respiratory secretions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2909, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-112', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with MDR-TB is prescribed the novel drug Bedaquiline. The nurse understands that this drug directly starves the bacteria of energy by inhibiting which specific target?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bedaquiline inhibits mycobacterial ATP synthase, particularly the c subunit, disrupting ATP production and bacterial energy metabolism.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2910, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-113', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the carina?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The carina is the ridge at the inferior end of the trachea where it divides into the right and left main bronchi.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2911, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-114', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is teaching a patient how to perform a \'directed cough.\' Which sequence is correct?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A directed cough involves a deep inspiration followed by glottic closure and forceful expiration, producing high airflow that helps mobilize secretions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2912, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-115', 'mcq', 'medium', 'It is estimated that Mycobacterium tuberculosis infects about what percentage of the world\'s population?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Approximately one-quarter of the world\'s population is estimated to have been infected with Mycobacterium tuberculosis, although most have latent rather than active disease.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2913, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-116', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which molecule has the greatest effect in controlling lung ventilation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Carbon dioxide has the greatest influence on ventilation because changes in arterial CO? alter hydrogen ion concentration and stimulate central chemoreceptors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2914, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-117', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which substance is identified as a potential trigger that can precipitate an acute episode of status asthmaticus?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aspirin can trigger bronchospasm in susceptible individuals, particularly those with aspirin-exacerbated respiratory disease, and may precipitate a severe asthma attack.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2915, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-118', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which intervention is the single most effective way to slow the progression of COPD?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Smoking cessation is the most effective intervention for slowing the progression of COPD and reducing further loss of lung function.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2916, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-119', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is a high-protein, high-calorie diet essential for a patient with a lung abscess?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chronic infection increases metabolic demands and causes a catabolic state. Adequate protein and calories support immune function and tissue repair.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2917, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-120', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with allergic rhinitis is prescribed ophthalmic agents. The nurse explains to the patient that this medication is intended to relieve which specific symptoms?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ophthalmic agents are applied to the eyes and are used to relieve ocular allergy symptoms such as itching, irritation, redness, and watering.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2918, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-121', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is a classic GI side effect of almost all expectorants mentioned in the note?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Expectorants can cause gastrointestinal irritation, with abdominal discomfort or cramping being a commonly reported adverse effect.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2919, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-122', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which molecule or ion dissolved in blood is able to stimulate the central chemoreceptors of the brain\'s respiratory centre?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Carbon dioxide readily crosses the blood-brain barrier and alters cerebrospinal fluid pH, thereby stimulating central chemoreceptors and increasing ventilation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2920, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-123', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a cold reports the sudden appearance of a painful blister on their lip. The nurse recognizes this as what common manifestation associated with viral rhinitis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A viral illness can trigger reactivation of herpes simplex virus, producing a painful cold sore around the lips.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2921, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-124', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient in the emergency department is experiencing a severe asthma exacerbation (status asthmaticus). The nurse prepares an intravenous infusion of Hydrocortisone. What is the primary cellular goal of this intervention?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hydrocortisone is a corticosteroid that reduces airway inflammation, mucosal edema, and bronchial hyper-reactivity; it does not provide immediate bronchodilation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2922, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-125', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The respiratory centre of the brain controls the respiratory muscles. Which of the following does NOT happen?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hydrogen ions do not readily cross the blood-brain barrier. Increased CO? crosses the barrier and changes CSF pH, stimulating central chemoreceptors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2923, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-126', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is a critical teaching point for a patient using an inhaled corticosteroid?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rinsing the mouth after using an inhaled corticosteroid reduces the risk of oral candidiasis and other local side effects.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2924, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-127', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a malignant effusion has a pleuroperitoneal shunt. What instruction should the nurse provide regarding its use?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pleuroperitoneal shunts generally require manual pumping of the reservoir to move pleural fluid into the peritoneal cavity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2925, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-128', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is a cavity in a skull bone that is lined with mucus membrane?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A sinus is an air-filled cavity within a skull bone lined by respiratory mucous membrane.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2926, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-129', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Normal expiration in a person at rest is due to:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Normal quiet expiration is passive and occurs mainly because of elastic recoil of the lungs and chest wall after inspiration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2927, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-130', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is a \'double lung transplant\' technique preferred for patients with end-stage cystic fibrosis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bilateral transplantation removes the chronically infected native lungs, reducing the risk of infection of a transplanted lung.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2928, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-131', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Occupational health nurses advise workers at risk for lung disease to receive which annual vaccination?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Annual influenza vaccination helps reduce the risk of serious respiratory infection and complications in people at increased risk of lung disease.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2929, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-132', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a lung abscess is too weak to cough effectively. What is the nurse\'s next best action to maintain airway patency?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'If the patient cannot clear secretions effectively, suctioning can help maintain airway patency and remove obstructing secretions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2930, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-133', 'mcq', 'medium', 'To assess for a positive Homans\' sign, the nurse should:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Homans\' sign is traditionally assessed by dorsiflexing the foot and observing for calf pain, although the test is not sufficiently reliable to diagnose DVT.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2931, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-134', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is interpreting a Mantoux test for a patient with HIV. The induration measures 7 mm. How should the nurse interpret this result?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'In people with HIV, an induration of 5 mm or greater is considered positive because of their increased risk of tuberculosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2932, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-135', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Upon assessment, the nurse notes severe swelling and redness around the patient\'s right eye (orbital cellulitis). The nurse knows this is:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Orbital cellulitis is an uncommon but potentially serious complication of sinus or facial infection and can threaten vision and spread intracranially.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2933, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-136', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Diagnostic confirmation of a lung abscess is made by:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Diagnosis and evaluation of a lung abscess may require imaging and microbiological studies, with chest imaging being particularly important for identifying the characteristic cavity and air-fluid level.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2934, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-137', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which antitussive is described as the \'standard\' against which others are compared?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Codeine has traditionally been used as the reference or standard antitussive against which the effectiveness of other cough suppressants is compared.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2935, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-138', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient experiencing an acute asthma attack reaches for their Sodium Cromoglycate metered-dose inhaler. Why must the nurse intervene and provide a different medication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sodium cromoglycate is primarily used for prevention and maintenance. It does not provide rapid bronchodilation during an acute asthma attack.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2936, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-139', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which surgical procedure involves removing a thick, fibrous exudate that is \'trapping\' the lung in a patient with empyema?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Decortication involves removing the thick fibrous pleural peel that restricts lung expansion in chronic empyema.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2937, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-140', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Acyclovir, an antiviral agent, is recommended for:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Acyclovir is an antiviral medication used to treat infections caused by herpes simplex virus, including oral and genital herpes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2938, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-141', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nursing management for a patient with acute pharyngitis includes:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Management may include rest, measures to relieve throat discomfort such as an ice collar, and a soft or liquid diet when swallowing is painful.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2939, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-142', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the primary clinical symptom of pulmonary hypertension that occurs initially with exertion?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dyspnea, particularly with exertion, is usually an early symptom of pulmonary hypertension due to reduced ability to increase cardiac output during activity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2940, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-143', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During a pharmacology review session, a nurse compares Ephedrine nasal drops and Dexamethasone nasal spray. Which statement accurately highlights their pharmacokinetic differences?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ephedrine is a sympathomimetic decongestant that produces relatively rapid nasal vasoconstriction, whereas dexamethasone reduces inflammation and has a slower therapeutic effect.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2941, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-144', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which combination of medications makes up the FDA-approved Nix-TB (BPaL) regimen used specifically for Extensively Drug-Resistant (XDR) TB?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The BPaL regimen consists of bedaquiline, pretomanid, and linezolid and is used for certain highly drug-resistant tuberculosis cases.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2942, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-145', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What are the membranes that surround each lung called?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The pleura consists of the visceral pleura covering the lung and the parietal pleura lining the thoracic cavity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2943, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-146', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is diagnosed with acute laryngitis. What is the most important instruction the nurse should provide regarding voice care?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Voice rest allows the inflamed vocal cords to heal. Whispering can actually strain the vocal cords and should not be used as a substitute for voice rest.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2944, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-147', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is responsible for increasing respiratory activity under normal conditions?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Increased blood CO? is the primary normal stimulus for increased ventilation through stimulation of central and peripheral chemoreceptors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2945, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-148', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which surgical procedure for laryngeal cancer involves the removal of the hyoid bone, glottis, and false cords while preserving the true vocal cords?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Supraglottic laryngectomy removes structures above the true vocal cords, including the epiglottis, false cords, and often the hyoid, while preserving the true vocal cords.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2946, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-149', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Thoracentesis is the indicated management for atelectasis caused by which underlying condition?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thoracentesis removes pleural fluid and relieves lung compression when a large pleural effusion causes atelectasis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2947, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-150', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse knows to assess a patient with pulmonary arterial hypertension for the primary symptom of:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dyspnea, particularly with exertion, is usually the earliest and most common symptom of pulmonary arterial hypertension.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2948, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-151', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A pharmacology researcher is developing a new drug that acts as an antagonist exclusively at the H3 and H4 receptors. Based on current clinical knowledge, what established therapeutic indication would this drug have?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'H3 and H4 receptors are recognized pharmacologic targets, but no established routine clinical indication is currently based on an H3/H4 antagonist used exclusively at both receptors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2949, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-152', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is an indwelling urinary catheter inserted for a patient with a massive embolism and hypotension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Urine output provides an important indicator of renal perfusion and overall circulatory status in a hypotensive patient.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2950, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-153', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the primary goal of pulmonary rehabilitation for a COPD patient?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pulmonary rehabilitation aims to improve exercise tolerance, functional capacity, symptom control, and independence rather than cure COPD.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2951, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-154', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which gas comprises 78% of atmospheric air?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Nitrogen makes up approximately 78% of Earth\'s atmosphere, while oxygen makes up about 21%.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2952, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-155', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which second-line antitubercular drug is structurally related to Isoniazid and also disrupts mycolic acid synthesis, requiring pyridoxine supplementation to prevent peripheral neuritis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ethionamide is structurally related to isoniazid, inhibits mycolic acid synthesis, and can cause peripheral neuropathy; pyridoxine may be given to reduce this risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2953, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-156', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A communication established between a bronchus and the pleural space is known as:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A bronchopleural fistula is an abnormal communication between a bronchus and the pleural space.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2954, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-157', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the therapeutic goal of using Positive End-Expiratory Pressure (PEEP) in ARDS management?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'PEEP maintains positive pressure at end expiration, helping recruit and keep alveoli open and improve oxygenation in ARDS.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2955, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-158', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is diagnosed with Small Cell Lung Cancer (SCLC). Which classification system will the healthcare team use to describe the extent of the disease?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'SCLC is traditionally classified as limited-stage or extensive-stage disease for treatment planning.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2956, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-159', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The greatest amount of air which can be moved in and out of the respiratory system is the:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vital capacity is the maximum amount of air that can be exhaled after a maximum inspiration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2957, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-160', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the specific purpose of percussing the sinuses using the index finger during assessment?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sinus percussion is performed to assess for tenderness or pain, which may suggest sinus inflammation or infection.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2958, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-161', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is considered the \'hallmark\' clinical characteristic of sarcoidosis onset?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sarcoidosis often develops insidiously and may be discovered incidentally because early disease can have few or no prominent symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2959, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-162', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why can bronchioles constrict while secondary bronchi cannot?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bronchioles contain smooth muscle but lack cartilage, allowing their diameter to change significantly; larger bronchi are supported by cartilage.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2960, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-163', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient maintained on oral Theophylline presents to the clinic with complaints of severe nausea, insomnia, and irritability. The nurse anticipates checking a serum theophylline level. At what serum concentration do these specific side effects typically begin to manifest?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Theophylline adverse effects such as nausea, insomnia, and irritability commonly begin as serum levels rise above the usual therapeutic range, around 10?15 mcg/mL.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2961, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-164', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a chronic smoker\'s cough is prescribed Carbocysteine. What specific assessment must accompany this medication therapy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Carbocysteine can cause gastrointestinal irritation, so patients should be monitored for significant gastrointestinal adverse effects.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2962, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-165', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient admits to using topical oxymetazoline (Afrin) nasal spray for the past 7 days to manage sinus congestion. Based on this history, what assessment finding should the nurse anticipate?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Prolonged use of topical nasal decongestants can cause rebound congestion, known as rhinitis medicamentosa.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2963, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-166', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient reports hoarseness lasting for three weeks and a persistent \'burning\' sensation when drinking orange juice. The nurse recognizes these as early signs of:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Persistent hoarseness, especially lasting more than a few weeks, is an important warning sign of laryngeal cancer and requires evaluation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2964, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-167', 'mcq', 'medium', 'For a patient being treated at home for an underlying infection, which teaching point regarding pharmacology is most critical?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Patients prescribed antibiotics should take them exactly as directed and complete the prescribed course unless instructed otherwise by their healthcare provider.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2965, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-168', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is caring for an asthmatic patient who develops a dry, hacking cough. Why is the nurse hesitant to administer Codeine?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Codeine suppresses the cough reflex, which can impair clearance of respiratory secretions and potentially contribute to airway obstruction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2966, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-169', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with bronchiectasis is prescribed postural drainage. What is the primary objective of this intervention?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Postural drainage uses gravity and positioning to facilitate movement and removal of retained bronchial secretions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2967, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-170', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with chronic pharyngitis works in a dusty factory and smokes a pack of cigarettes daily. Which type of pharyngitis, characterized by a thin, glistening, and wrinkled membrane, is likely to develop?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Atrophic chronic pharyngitis causes thinning and atrophy of the pharyngeal mucosa, producing a thin, dry, glistening and wrinkled appearance.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2968, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-171', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which arterial blood gas (ABG) values meet the clinical criteria for a diagnosis of Acute Respiratory Failure (ARF)?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe hypoxemia and hypercapnia with acidemia are consistent with acute respiratory failure, particularly when PaO? is below about 60 mmHg and PaCO? is elevated.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2969, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-172', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A molecule that is important in maintaining normal lung structure is:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pulmonary surfactant reduces surface tension and prevents alveolar collapse, helping maintain normal lung structure and function.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2970, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-173', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is NOT in direct contact with the parietal pleura?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The lung is covered by the visceral pleura, whereas the parietal pleura lines the thoracic wall, diaphragm, and mediastinal structures.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2971, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-174', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The most common surgical procedure for a small, apparently curable tumor of the lung is a:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lobectomy, removal of the affected lung lobe, is commonly performed for a localized resectable lung tumor when the patient\'s condition permits.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2972, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-175', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is teaching a patient about self-care for acute sinusitis. Which patient statement indicates a need for further teaching?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Stopping an antibiotic when symptoms improve can lead to incomplete treatment and recurrence or resistance; the patient should follow the prescribed regimen.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2973, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-176', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with an established history of severe asthma is admitted with a hypertensive crisis. The physician considers starting a beta-blocker. Which medication class is strictly contraindicated due to the risk of triggering severe bronchospasm?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Non-selective beta-blockers block beta-2 receptors in bronchial smooth muscle and can cause severe bronchospasm in patients with asthma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2974, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-177', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient in the emergency department is receiving continuous, high-dose Salbutamol nebulization for an acute asthma exacerbation. Which laboratory value must the nurse monitor most closely during this therapy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'High-dose salbutamol can shift potassium into cells and cause hypokalemia, so serum potassium should be monitored closely.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2975, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-178', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with centrilobular emphysema is likely to show which clinical sign?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Centrilobular emphysema is classically associated with a thin or lean appearance, dyspnea, and pursed-lip breathing, traditionally described as a \"pink puffer.\"', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2976, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-179', 'mcq', 'medium', 'More than 80% of all lung cancers are primarily caused by:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cigarette smoking is the major preventable cause of lung cancer and accounts for the large majority of cases.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2977, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-180', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient taking Pretomanid reports persistent nausea, abdominal pain, and visual changes. Upon reviewing their recent lab work, the nurse notes a blood glucose level of 55 mg/dL. Are these findings related to the medication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pretomanid-containing TB regimens can cause gastrointestinal adverse effects and metabolic abnormalities; the described combination is treated in the question as medication-related.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2978, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-181', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is assessing a patient with a large pleural effusion. Which finding should the nurse expect during percussion of the affected area?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Fluid in the pleural space produces a dull or flat percussion note over the affected area.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2979, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-182', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Insidious onset of alveolar collapse in a patient where a tumor is slowly compressing the airways is classified as:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Slow obstruction and compression of the airway by a tumor can produce chronic atelectasis, characterized by gradual alveolar collapse.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2980, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-183', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following describes the relationship between the trachea and the oesophagus?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The esophagus lies posterior to the trachea, and the membranous posterior wall of the trachea is closely related to it.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2981, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-184', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a total laryngectomy is concerned about the risk of aspiration. How should the nurse explain the new anatomical structure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'After total laryngectomy, the airway is permanently separated from the digestive tract and the patient breathes through a permanent stoma, eliminating aspiration through the airway.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2982, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-185', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is Ammonium Chloride strictly contraindicated in a patient with a history of severe hepatic impairment?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ammonium chloride is metabolized in the liver and can increase ammonia-related toxicity, making it unsuitable in severe hepatic impairment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2983, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-186', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which clinical sign is associated with right ventricular failure in Cor Pulmonale?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Right-sided heart failure causes systemic venous congestion, producing peripheral edema, jugular venous distention, and hepatomegaly.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2984, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-187', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which intervention is classified as a \'first-line\' measure to minimize or treat atelectasis by improving ventilation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Frequent repositioning, early ambulation, deep breathing, coughing, and incentive spirometry are first-line measures to improve ventilation and prevent or treat atelectasis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2985, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-188', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with severe motion sickness is preparing for a boat trip and is prescribed oral Promethazine. To achieve optimal efficacy, what administration timing should the nurse recommend?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Promethazine is most effective for motion sickness when administered prophylactically, generally about 30?60 minutes before travel.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2986, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-189', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient asks how guaifenesin (Robitussin) will help their sinus pain. What is the nurse\'s best response?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Guaifenesin is an expectorant that helps loosen and thin respiratory secretions, making them easier to clear and reducing congestion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2987, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-190', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which organism is commonly associated with lung abscesses in patients with predisposing factors?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lung abscesses may involve mixed bacterial infections, including Staphylococcus aureus and Klebsiella, particularly in patients with aspiration or other predisposing conditions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2988, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-191', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How is the diaphragm innervated?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The diaphragm is primarily innervated by the phrenic nerves arising from spinal nerve roots C3, C4, and C5.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2989, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-192', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which clinical finding is specifically characteristic of advanced pulmonary edema when fluid mixes with air in the alveoli?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe pulmonary edema can produce pink or blood-tinged frothy sputum as fluid mixes with air and small amounts of blood in the alveoli.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2990, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-193', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is assessing a patient with empyema. Which finding is consistent with this condition during physical examination?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Empyema is a collection of pus in the pleural space and commonly causes decreased or absent breath sounds with dullness to percussion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2991, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-194', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Surfactant:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pulmonary surfactant reduces surface tension within the alveoli, helping prevent alveolar collapse, especially at the end of expiration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2992, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-195', 'mcq', 'medium', 'An adult patient is prescribed Pseudoephedrine 60 mg orally for systemic relief of cold symptoms. The nurse monitors the patient and expects the drug to be well absorbed and reach peak serum levels within what timeframe?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Oral pseudoephedrine is rapidly absorbed, with peak plasma concentrations generally reached about 1?2 hours after administration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2993, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-196', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with acute asthma is experiencing severe wheezing and difficulty speaking. Which medication should the nurse expect to administer first for rapid bronchodilation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Salbutamol is a short-acting beta-2 agonist that produces rapid bronchodilation during acute asthma attacks.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2994, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-197', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which assessment finding is most characteristic of a patient experiencing an acute asthma attack?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Airway narrowing in asthma commonly produces expiratory wheezing due to difficulty moving air through constricted bronchi.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2995, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-198', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which position is most helpful for a patient experiencing severe dyspnea?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'High-Fowler\'s position promotes maximum lung expansion and reduces the work of breathing.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2996, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-199', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is teaching a patient how to use a metered-dose inhaler. What should the patient do immediately before inhaling the medication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Exhaling fully before inhalation allows the patient to take a deeper breath and deliver more medication into the lower airways.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2997, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-200', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which condition is characterized by irreversible airflow limitation and destruction of alveolar walls?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Emphysema involves permanent enlargement of air spaces and destruction of alveolar walls, resulting in irreversible airflow limitation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2998, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-201', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the primary risk factor for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cigarette smoking is the major preventable risk factor for COPD.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(2999, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-202', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which finding is most suggestive of hypoxemia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cyanosis may occur when oxygen saturation is significantly reduced and is an important clinical sign of hypoxemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3000, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-203', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with COPD is prescribed oxygen therapy. Why is controlled oxygen administration important?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Some patients with severe COPD may retain carbon dioxide, so oxygen is carefully titrated to achieve the prescribed saturation without excessive administration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3001, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-204', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which breathing technique is commonly taught to patients with COPD to improve expiration?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pursed-lip breathing slows expiration and helps maintain airway pressure, reducing airway collapse and air trapping.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3002, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-205', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which complication is commonly associated with prolonged COPD?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chronic hypoxemia and pulmonary hypertension in COPD can lead to right ventricular failure, known as cor pulmonale.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3003, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-206', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which test is commonly used to evaluate airflow obstruction in COPD?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Spirometry measures airflow and lung volumes and is central to diagnosing and assessing obstructive lung disease.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3004, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-207', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with pneumonia has thick respiratory secretions. Which nursing intervention best promotes secretion clearance?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Adequate hydration helps thin respiratory secretions, making them easier to expectorate.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3005, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-208', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which organism is a common cause of community-acquired bacterial pneumonia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Streptococcus pneumoniae is one of the most common causes of community-acquired bacterial pneumonia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3006, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-209', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which assessment finding is expected in a patient with pneumonia involving consolidation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Consolidated lung tissue can transmit bronchial sounds and produce crackles during auscultation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3007, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-210', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with pneumonia develops pleuritic chest pain. What does pleuritic pain typically worsen with?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Inflamed pleural surfaces cause sharp pain that is typically aggravated by deep inspiration and coughing.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3008, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-211', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which nursing intervention is most appropriate for a patient with pneumonia and fever?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Fluids help maintain hydration, while monitoring temperature helps assess infection and response to treatment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3009, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-212', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which drug class is commonly used to treat bacterial pneumonia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Antibiotics are used when pneumonia is caused by susceptible bacteria.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3010, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-213', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with tuberculosis is prescribed several medications simultaneously. What is the primary reason for multidrug therapy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Using multiple effective antitubercular drugs reduces the risk of Mycobacterium tuberculosis developing resistance.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3011, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-214', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which medication is commonly included in first-line treatment for tuberculosis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rifampicin is one of the core first-line antitubercular medications.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3012, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-215', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient taking rifampicin should be taught that the drug may cause:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rifampicin can cause harmless orange-red discoloration of urine, tears, sweat, and other body fluids.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3013, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-216', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which adverse effect should a nurse monitor for in a patient receiving isoniazid?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Isoniazid can cause peripheral neuropathy, and pyridoxine supplementation is often used to reduce this risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3014, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-217', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which vitamin is commonly administered with isoniazid?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pyridoxine, or vitamin B6, helps prevent isoniazid-associated peripheral neuropathy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3015, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-218', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient taking ethambutol should be monitored for which adverse effect?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ethambutol can cause optic neuritis, so visual acuity and color vision should be monitored.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3016, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-219', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which instruction is most important for a patient taking ethambutol?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Visual changes can indicate optic toxicity and should be reported promptly.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3017, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-220', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient taking pyrazinamide should have which laboratory parameter monitored?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pyrazinamide can cause hepatotoxicity, so liver function should be monitored.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3018, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-221', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which respiratory condition is caused by an accumulation of air in the pleural space?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A pneumothorax occurs when air enters the pleural space and may cause partial or complete lung collapse.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3019, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-222', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which emergency condition is characterized by pressure progressively increasing within the pleural space?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tension pneumothorax causes increasing intrapleural pressure, compressing the lung and potentially impairing venous return.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3020, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-223', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is an important emergency intervention for tension pneumothorax?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Needle decompression rapidly releases trapped pleural air and is an emergency treatment for tension pneumothorax.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3021, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-224', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which assessment finding may occur with pneumothorax on the affected side?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Air in the pleural space can prevent normal transmission of breath sounds, producing decreased or absent sounds on the affected side.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3022, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-225', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which condition involves accumulation of fluid in the pleural space?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pleural effusion is an abnormal collection of fluid between the pleural layers.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3023, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-226', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which procedure may be performed to remove fluid from a pleural effusion?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thoracentesis involves inserting a needle into the pleural space to remove fluid for therapeutic or diagnostic purposes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3024, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-227', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What should the nurse monitor after thoracentesis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pneumothorax is a possible complication after thoracentesis, so respiratory status and breath sounds should be closely monitored.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3025, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-228', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which condition is characterized by pus within the pleural cavity?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Empyema is a collection of infected purulent fluid in the pleural space.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3026, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-229', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which disorder is characterized by permanent dilation of the bronchi?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bronchiectasis involves irreversible dilation and structural damage to the bronchi, often associated with chronic infection and retained secretions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3027, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-230', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is a major clinical problem in bronchiectasis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Damaged and dilated bronchi retain mucus, increasing the risk of infection and recurrent respiratory symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3028, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-231', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which intervention helps a patient with bronchiectasis clear respiratory secretions?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chest physiotherapy, including postural drainage and airway-clearance techniques, assists removal of retained secretions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3029, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-232', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which condition is characterized by inflammation of the pleura?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pleurisy is inflammation of the pleural membranes and commonly causes sharp chest pain worsened by breathing.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3030, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-233', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which symptom is commonly associated with laryngeal cancer?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Persistent hoarseness is an important warning sign of laryngeal cancer, particularly when it lasts several weeks.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3031, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-234', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which lifestyle factor significantly increases the risk of laryngeal cancer?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tobacco exposure is a major risk factor for laryngeal cancer.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3032, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-235', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which procedure creates a surgical opening in the trachea to establish an airway?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A tracheostomy creates an opening through the neck into the trachea to provide an alternative airway.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3033, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-236', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is an important nursing intervention for a patient with a tracheostomy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Maintaining airway patency through appropriate suctioning, humidification, and tube care is essential.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3034, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-237', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which complication can occur when a tracheostomy becomes obstructed by thick secretions?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thick secretions can obstruct the tracheostomy tube and cause acute respiratory distress.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3035, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-238', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which device is commonly used to estimate peripheral oxygen saturation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A pulse oximeter provides a noninvasive estimate of arterial oxygen saturation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3036, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-239', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which oxygen-delivery device can provide a precise concentration of oxygen?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A Venturi mask delivers a controlled and relatively precise fraction of inspired oxygen.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3037, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-240', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which oxygen-delivery device is commonly used when a high concentration of oxygen is urgently required in a spontaneously breathing patient?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A non-rebreather mask can deliver a high concentration of oxygen when properly fitted and supplied with adequate flow.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3038, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-241', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which medication is a long-acting beta-2 agonist used for maintenance treatment of asthma or COPD?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Salmeterol is a long-acting beta-2 agonist used for maintenance bronchodilation and is not intended for rapid relief of acute asthma symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3039, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-242', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which medication is classified as an inhaled corticosteroid?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Budesonide is an inhaled corticosteroid that reduces airway inflammation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3040, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-243', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What instruction should a patient follow after using an inhaled corticosteroid?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rinsing the mouth after inhaled corticosteroids reduces the risk of oral candidiasis and irritation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3041, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-244', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which drug is an inhaled anticholinergic commonly used in COPD?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ipratropium blocks muscarinic receptors and produces bronchodilation, making it useful in COPD.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3042, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-245', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which adverse effect can occur with inhaled ipratropium?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Anticholinergic effects of ipratropium commonly include dry mouth.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3043, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-246', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which medication is a leukotriene receptor antagonist?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Montelukast blocks leukotriene receptors and is used as a controller medication in asthma and allergic rhinitis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3044, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-247', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which drug is commonly used as a mucolytic to reduce the viscosity of respiratory secretions?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Acetylcysteine breaks disulfide bonds in mucus and helps make thick respiratory secretions easier to clear.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3045, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-248', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which precaution is important when administering acetylcysteine to a patient with asthma?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Acetylcysteine can occasionally cause bronchospasm, so patients with asthma require careful respiratory monitoring.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3046, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-249', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which medication is classified as an expectorant?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Guaifenesin is an expectorant that helps loosen respiratory secretions and facilitates coughing.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3047, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-250', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which class of drug is primarily used to suppress a troublesome nonproductive cough?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Antitussives reduce the cough reflex and are mainly used for troublesome dry, nonproductive coughs.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3048, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-251', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which finding may indicate respiratory failure in a deteriorating patient?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe hypoxemia is a major indicator of respiratory failure and requires urgent assessment and intervention.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3049, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-252', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which arterial blood gas value represents normal arterial oxygen tension approximately?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A normal arterial PaO? is generally about 80?100 mmHg in a healthy adult breathing room air at sea level.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3050, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-253', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which ABG value represents normal arterial carbon dioxide tension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Normal arterial PaCO? is approximately 35?45 mmHg.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3051, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-254', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with COPD has a PaCO? of 60 mmHg. This finding indicates:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A PaCO? above the normal range indicates hypercapnia, reflecting inadequate alveolar ventilation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3052, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-255', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which acid-base disorder may result from acute respiratory hypoventilation with carbon dioxide retention?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hypoventilation causes carbon dioxide retention, increasing carbonic acid and producing respiratory acidosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3053, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-256', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is hyperventilating due to anxiety. Which ABG change is expected initially?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rapid ventilation removes excess carbon dioxide, causing PaCO? to fall and producing respiratory alkalosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3054, 9, 34, NULL, 'AC-NG-257', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which structure prevents food from entering the trachea during swallowing?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The epiglottis folds over the laryngeal inlet during swallowing and helps direct food away from the airway.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:01:11', '2026-10-10 15:01:11', NULL),
(3057, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-03', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient has been on a sodium nitroprusside infusion for 48 hours. The nurse notes the patient is becoming increasingly disoriented and reporting profound weakness. The nurse suspects which complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sodium nitroprusside can produce cyanide or thiocyanate toxicity, especially with prolonged infusion. Neurologic changes, confusion, weakness, and metabolic abnormalities may occur.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3058, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-04', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The cystic vein drains the:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The cystic vein drains blood from the gallbladder, eventually contributing to the portal venous circulation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3059, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-05', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse notices a sudden drop in a patient\'s platelet count after five days of Heparin therapy. What is the suspected complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A significant platelet fall after several days of heparin therapy is characteristic of heparin-induced thrombocytopenia, an immune-mediated complication that can cause thrombosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3060, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-06', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mrs. Balogun is admitted to the intensive care unit with acute hypertensive encephalopathy and a diastolic blood pressure of 155 mm Hg. What is the precise, time-sensitive hemodynamic target for pharmacological intervention in this acute crisis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'In hypertensive emergencies, blood pressure should be lowered carefully rather than normalized immediately. Rapid excessive reduction can cause cerebral, renal, or coronary hypoperfusion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3061, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-07', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which clinical finding in the eyes indicates severe or uncontrolled hypertension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Papilledema indicates optic-disc swelling caused by markedly increased intracranial pressure and may occur with severe hypertension.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3062, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-08', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nurse Fatima assesses an unresponsive 6-year-old child in the pediatric ward. She palpates a brachial pulse and notes a heart rate of 55 beats per minute. What is the most appropriate immediate physical action regarding circulation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'In an unresponsive child with severe bradycardia and signs of poor circulation, chest compressions are indicated when the heart rate remains below 60/min despite effective ventilation and signs of poor perfusion are present.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3063, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-09', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Chief Okeke has lived with uncontrolled \'silent killer\' disease for two decades. He now reports experiencing severe leg cramping when walking short distances, which resolves with rest. This specific symptom (intermittent claudication) signifies advanced damage to which respective target organ system?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Intermittent claudication is a manifestation of peripheral arterial disease caused by reduced blood flow through the arteries of the limbs.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3064, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-10', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which reversible cause of PEA should the nurse investigate?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cardiac tamponade is one of the reversible causes of pulseless electrical activity and should be rapidly identified and treated during resuscitation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3065, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-11', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient in hypertensive emergency is prescribed Sodium Nitroprusside. What is a key characteristic of this drug?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sodium nitroprusside is an intravenous vasodilator with an extremely rapid onset and short duration of action, allowing close titration of blood pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3066, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-12', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is true of complete cardiac diastole?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'During diastole, the heart chambers relax and fill. Blood flows into the atria and passes through open atrioventricular valves into the ventricles.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3067, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-13', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with an inoperable insulinoma is prescribed oral diazoxide. The nurse understands this medication is indicated because it:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Diazoxide raises blood glucose primarily by inhibiting insulin release from pancreatic beta cells, making it useful for hypoglycemia associated with insulinoma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3068, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-14', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following arteries do NOT arise from the ascending aorta?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The left subclavian artery arises from the aortic arch, not the ascending aorta. The ascending aorta itself gives rise to the coronary arteries.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3069, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-15', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mrs. Ibe presents to the emergency room with acute left ventricular failure, acute pulmonary edema, and a diastolic blood pressure of 145 mm Hg. A junior staff member suggests sublingual administration of fast-acting nifedipine to rapidly lower the pressure. Why must this intervention be strictly avoided?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Immediate-release sublingual nifedipine can cause an unpredictable and excessively rapid fall in blood pressure, potentially producing cerebral or coronary ischemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3070, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-16', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mrs. Okafor, a 48-year-old female with a history of ulcerative colitis, presents to the A&E with classic STEMI symptoms that started 40 minutes ago. The cardiology team is evaluating her for pharmacological reperfusion. Which specific thrombolytic agent is contraindicated in her case based on her medical history?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Streptokinase is a thrombolytic agent and active or recent significant gastrointestinal bleeding can make thrombolytic therapy contraindicated. The question identifies streptokinase as the intended agent.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3071, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-17', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A pregnant patient is admitted with preeclampsia. The nurse anticipates an order for which combined alpha and beta blocker that is commonly used for pregnancy-induced hypertension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Labetalol blocks both alpha-1 and beta adrenergic receptors and is commonly used to control hypertension during pregnancy, including severe hypertension associated with preeclampsia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3072, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-18', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which physical assessment finding is the most important diagnostic indicator of an abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA)?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A pulsatile abdominal mass is a classic physical finding associated with an abdominal aortic aneurysm.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3073, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-19', 'mcq', 'medium', 'After administering atropine to a patient with bradycardia, the nurse assesses for therapeutic effectiveness by:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Atropine blocks parasympathetic effects on the heart and is used to increase heart rate in symptomatic bradycardia. An increased heart rate indicates therapeutic response.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3074, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-20', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient\'s coronary plaque has a thin fibrous cap and a large lipid core. What is the primary clinical concern?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A thin fibrous cap and large lipid core characterize a vulnerable plaque, which has an increased risk of rupture and subsequent thrombus formation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3075, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-21', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During a physical exam, the nurse notes a systolic \'mitral click.\' This finding is the hallmark sign for:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A systolic click, particularly a mid-systolic click, is characteristic of mitral valve prolapse and results from abnormal movement of the mitral valve during systole.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3076, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-22', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Ms. Zainab is initiated on a central/autonomic ganglion adrenergic blocker for moderate hypertension, prescribed at 0.5-2 g/day in divided doses. She also takes medication for a psychiatric condition. Which class of drugs must she avoid due to an absolute contraindication with her new antihypertensive?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ganglion-blocking antihypertensive drugs can have important interactions with tricyclic antidepressants, which may alter their antihypertensive effects and increase adverse effects.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3077, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-23', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Chief Odunze suddenly collapses at a town hall meeting. A nurse in the audience rushes over. She notes he is unresponsive, profoundly pallid, and has cold, clammy skin. Which combination of additional clinical signs would definitively confirm a clinical diagnosis of cardiac arrest requiring immediate CPR?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cardiac arrest is identified by unresponsiveness, absence of a normal pulse, and absent or abnormal breathing such as agonal gasping. These findings require immediate CPR.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3078, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-24', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Amina experiences severe chest pain that is unresponsive to 0.3 mg sublingual nitroglycerin and subsequent doses of IV diamorphine. The physician decides to administer a different intravenous agent very slowly at a dose of 0.5 g to help relieve the pain. Which medication is being administered?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The supplied question identifies aminophylline as the intended answer. However, the stated dose and indication should be independently reviewed because the wording does not correspond well with standard acute coronary syndrome analgesic treatment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3079, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-25', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the definition of sinus tachycardia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sinus tachycardia is a sinus rhythm with a heart rate above 100 beats per minute. The rhythm remains sinus in origin.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3080, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-26', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The fibular artery is a branch of the:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The fibular artery, also called the peroneal artery, is a branch of the posterior tibial artery.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3081, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-27', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is started on Captopril. During therapy, the patient notices a metallic taste distortion. What is the appropriate nursing action?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Taste disturbance or dysgeusia is a recognized adverse effect of captopril and other ACE inhibitors. The finding should be documented and monitored.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3082, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-28', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following definitions best describes veins?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Veins are blood vessels that carry blood toward the heart. They may carry either oxygenated or deoxygenated blood depending on their location.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3083, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-29', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which patient history finding is an absolute contraindication for a scheduled Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) study?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A non-MRI-compatible implanted cardiac pacemaker can be a contraindication to MRI because the magnetic field can interfere with the device. Some modern pacemakers are MRI-conditional, so device compatibility must be confirmed.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3084, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-30', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is a precipitous drop in blood pressure dangerous during the treatment of a hypertensive crisis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'An excessively rapid fall in blood pressure can reduce perfusion to vital organs, including the brain, heart, and kidneys, potentially causing ischemia and shock.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3085, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-31', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is assessing a patient with cellulitis. Which finding would be considered a systemic manifestation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tender and enlarged regional lymph nodes reflect lymphatic involvement and are considered a manifestation beyond the immediate site of infection.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3086, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-32', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is checking the retinas of a hypertensive patient. What finding suggests vascular damage?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cotton-wool spots represent small retinal nerve-fiber layer infarctions and are associated with hypertensive vascular damage.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3087, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-33', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How many readings are required to officially diagnose hypertension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hypertension diagnosis generally requires repeated blood-pressure measurements rather than relying on one isolated elevated reading. The question\'s intended answer is an average of multiple readings over multiple visits.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3088, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-34', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nurse Fatima is monitoring the pupils of a patient undergoing CPR. She notes that the pupils remain widely dilated despite continuous compressions. What specific pathophysiological state does this pupillary response indicate according to the monitoring guidelines?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Persistent widely dilated pupils during cardiac arrest can indicate severe cerebral hypoxia and possible brain injury, although pupillary findings alone do not determine neurological outcome during CPR.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3089, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-35', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is monitoring a patient receiving Alteplase (t-PA). Which nursing action is part of \'bleeding precautions\'?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Alteplase increases the risk of bleeding. Minimizing invasive procedures and unnecessary venipunctures reduces the risk of bleeding complications.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3090, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-36', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During a community health screening, Mr. Balogun is found to have a blood pressure of 165/105 mm Hg. He is completely asymptomatic. Before initiating a lifelong pharmacological regimen, the clinical protocol mandates confirming the diagnosis. What is the precise diagnostic requirement for establishing sustained hypertension in this scenario?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The question\'s intended answer is repeated elevated blood-pressure measurements over several days. In clinical practice, diagnosis should be based on properly measured repeated readings on separate occasions or validated out-of-office measurements.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3091, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-37', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Enlargement and inflammation of a lymph node is called:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lymphadenopathy refers to enlargement or abnormality of lymph nodes. Lymphadenitis specifically refers to inflammation of a lymph node.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3092, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-38', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following statements best describes the safety profile of cardiac glycosides like Digoxin?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Digoxin has a narrow therapeutic index, meaning there is a relatively small difference between therapeutic and toxic concentrations. Patients require careful monitoring for toxicity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3093, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-39', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 45-year-old patient with an acute myocardial infarction develops Ventricular Fibrillation (VF). The resuscitation team immediately initiates CPR and prepares for defibrillation. According to the specific shock cycles outlined, what is the correct energy sequence for the initial group of three shocks if the VF persists?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The intended sequence in the question is 200 J, 200 J, then 360 J. Defibrillation energy recommendations depend on whether a monophasic or biphasic defibrillator is being used.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3094, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-40', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the clinical significance of a patient\'s angina changing from \'stable\' to \'unstable\'?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Unstable angina is associated with plaque disruption and increased coronary thrombosis risk. It is an acute coronary syndrome and may precede myocardial infarction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3095, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-41', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient in hypertensive urgency is being treated with oral agents. Which class does Clonidine belong to?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Clonidine is a centrally acting alpha-2 adrenergic agonist. It reduces sympathetic outflow from the central nervous system and lowers blood pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3096, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-42', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse reviews the medication list of a patient with peripheral vascular disease and notes: Aspirin, Clopidogrel, and Vitamin E. What is the cumulative pharmacological effect of this specific combination?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aspirin and clopidogrel inhibit platelet aggregation, while vitamin E may also increase bleeding tendency. Together, the combination may increase protection against arterial thrombosis but also increases bleeding risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3097, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-43', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The tricuspid valve separates which two structures?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The tricuspid valve lies between the right atrium and right ventricle and prevents backflow of blood into the right atrium during ventricular systole.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3098, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-44', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the role of macrophages in the development of atherosclerosis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Macrophages take up oxidized LDL within the arterial wall and become foam cells, contributing to the formation and progression of atherosclerotic plaques.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3099, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-45', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Following a Transesophageal Echocardiogram (TEE), what is the nurse\'s priority assessment before allowing the patient to drink water?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'After TEE, the throat may remain anesthetized. The gag and cough reflexes must return before oral intake to reduce the risk of aspiration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3100, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-46', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Dr. Alabi is managing a patient with primary hypertension complicated by severe, chronic asthma. He needs to add an antihypertensive agent to lower peripheral vascular resistance. Which specific medication class is absolutely contraindicated due to the patient\'s respiratory status?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Non-selective beta-blockers can cause bronchoconstriction by blocking beta-2 receptors and may worsen asthma. Therefore, beta-blockers require particular caution or avoidance in severe asthma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3101, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-47', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient asks the nurse to explain the difference between arteriosclerosis and atherosclerosis. Which statement is most accurate?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Atherosclerosis is a form of arteriosclerosis characterized by lipid accumulation and plaque formation within the arterial intima.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3102, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-48', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Dr. Suleiman successfully resuscitates a patient from a prolonged episode of ventricular fibrillation. Moving directly into Phase II of the management protocol, what is the primary diagnostic aim the medical team must achieve to prevent recurrence?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'After successful resuscitation, identifying and treating the underlying reversible or correctable cause is important to prevent recurrence of the cardiac arrest.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3103, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-49', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Following the successful resuscitation of a 45-year-old male, the critical care protocol dictates meticulous body temperature management in the CICU. What is the explicit therapeutic goal regarding body temperature in Phase III?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Current post-cardiac-arrest care emphasizes active temperature control and prevention or treatment of fever. Routine cooling to exactly 32?C for all patients is not universally required.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3104, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-50', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Madam Ngozi is admitted with severe eclampsia and a diastolic blood pressure of 145 mmHg. The physician orders a fast-acting intravenous vasodilator specifically indicated for her presentation. Which of the following is the most appropriate agent and dosage based on the acute management protocol?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hydralazine is an established intravenous antihypertensive option for severe hypertension associated with preeclampsia or eclampsia. The dose is titrated according to the clinical response and protocol.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3105, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-51', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 60-year-old patient, Ngozi, is administered an intravenous infusion of a medication aimed at reducing myocardial oxygen consumption. The initial dose is 5 mg IV given every 5-10 minutes, with gradual escalation up to 50 mg once daily. The nurse must monitor her closely because she has a history of left ventricular dysfunction, which is a contraindication. Which drug is being administered?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Metoprolol is a beta-blocker that reduces heart rate and myocardial oxygen demand. It can worsen acute or decompensated left ventricular failure and therefore requires caution or contraindication in that setting.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3106, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-52', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with mild to moderate hypertension is prescribed Diltiazem. To prevent severe cardiovascular toxicity, the prescribing physician must ensure the patient\'s divided doses never exceed what absolute maximum daily limit?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The intended maximum in the question is 360 mg per day for the stated divided-dose regimen. Diltiazem maximum doses can vary according to the formulation, so the specific preparation must be considered.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3107, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-53', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Dr. Sani is teaching a BLS course. He emphasizes that the \'B\' in the ABC approach stands for Breathing. If mouth-to-mouth breathing fails to inflate the lungs after assessing airway clearance, how many rescue breaths should the rescuer attempt to give?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'When attempting rescue breathing, the rescuer should give two breaths after opening the airway, with each breath delivered over about one second and enough to produce visible chest rise.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3108, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-54', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse is preparing to administer adenosine. What is the correct technique for intravenous administration of this medication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Adenosine has an extremely short half-life and must be administered as a rapid IV bolus followed immediately by a rapid saline flush.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3109, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-55', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is preparing a patient for an exercise stress test. Which instruction is correct?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Patients are commonly instructed to avoid food for several hours and avoid stimulants such as caffeine and tobacco before the test. Some medications, including beta-blockers, may also need to be withheld according to the test protocol.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3110, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-56', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During a thoracotomy and internal cardiac massage, what preceding surgical or medical failure justifies this extreme, invasive intervention according to the protocol?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thoracotomy and internal cardiac massage are extreme resuscitative measures considered only after appropriate basic and advanced resuscitation measures have failed in selected circumstances.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3111, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-57', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is transitioned from Lisinopril to Losartan. The nurse explains that the primary benefit of Losartan regarding respiratory comfort is:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'ACE inhibitors such as lisinopril can increase bradykinin and cause a persistent dry cough. Losartan is an ARB and does not inhibit bradykinin breakdown, so cough is less common.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3112, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-58', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient suddenly stops taking their blood pressure medication. What are they at high risk for developing?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Suddenly discontinuing some antihypertensive medications can cause rebound hypertension, which may become severe and result in a hypertensive crisis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3113, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-59', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a suspected MI has a normal initial ECG. Does this rule out an MI?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A normal initial ECG does not exclude myocardial infarction. ECG changes can evolve, so serial ECGs and cardiac biomarkers may be required when clinical suspicion remains.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(3114, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-60', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 28-year-old female, Ngozi, presents to the A&E with palpitations and chest pain. Her heart rate is 210 bpm and regular. Her blood pressure is stable at 110/70 mmHg. The diagnosis is Paroxysmal Supraventricular Tachycardia (PSVT). What is the appropriate initial general measure before resorting to emergency pharmacological or electrical interventions?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'In a stable patient with regular PSVT, vagal manoeuvres are attempted first to increase vagal tone and potentially terminate the tachycardia. Carotid sinus massage is one historical example, although modified Valsalva is generally preferred in current practice.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3115, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-61', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Amina, a 45-year-old female, is admitted to the emergency department with sudden, severe chest pain that radiates to her back. She has a history of uncontrolled hypertension. Based on the cardiovascular causes of chest pain, which of the following is a potential life-threatening etiology that must be considered?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sudden severe chest pain radiating to the back in a patient with uncontrolled hypertension is concerning for aortic dissection, a life-threatening cardiovascular emergency.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3116, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-62', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient on a loop diuretic faces ototoxicity risks if they have:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Loop diuretics, particularly when given at high doses or rapidly intravenously, can cause ototoxicity. Patients with renal impairment are at increased risk because drug clearance may be reduced.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3117, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-63', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How is ET tube placement confirmed using a secondary method?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'End-tidal CO2 detection is a reliable secondary method for confirming tracheal intubation after initial clinical assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3118, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-64', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 70-year-old patient with a history of heart failure is prescribed Enoxaparin during a hospital admission for unstable angina. What is the route and frequency of administration for this anticoagulant?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Enoxaparin for unstable angina is commonly administered subcutaneously at 1 mg/kg every 12 hours.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3119, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-65', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During a supervised walk, a patient is told to use the \'talk test.\' What does this mean?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The talk test helps assess exercise intensity; inability to speak comfortably suggests that exercise intensity is too high.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3120, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-66', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with cellulitis of the left leg should be instructed to position the limb:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Elevating the affected limb above heart level helps reduce edema and promotes venous and lymphatic drainage.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3121, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-67', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Nnamdi presents with a resting blood pressure of 165/102 mm Hg. Before initiating a comprehensive pharmacological regimen, the clinical team conducts extensive ophthalmic, cardiac, and renal evaluations. What is the primary clinical rationale for this meticulous assessment phase?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Evaluation of the eyes, heart, and kidneys helps identify target-organ damage and determine the severity and appropriate management of hypertension.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3122, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-68', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How are cardiac cells mechanically attached to each other?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Intercalated discs provide mechanical attachment between cardiac muscle cells, while gap junctions provide electrical coupling.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3123, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-69', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In the lifestyle management of hypertension, alcohol intake for men should be limited to:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Traditional hypertension lifestyle recommendations limit alcohol intake in men to no more than about 2 standard drinks daily, approximately 1 oz (30 mL) of ethanol.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3124, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-70', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with heart failure asks why they must avoid NSAIDs like ibuprofen. The nurse\'s best response is:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'NSAIDs promote sodium and water retention, increase systemic vascular resistance, and can reduce renal perfusion, potentially worsening heart failure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3125, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-71', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Amina collapses in the hospital corridor. The responding nurse determines she is pulseless and immediately begins CPR. After one minute of cycles, what specific action must the nurse take according to the \'Reassessment\' protocol?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'After a period of CPR, the patient should be reassessed for return of spontaneous circulation and breathing according to the applicable resuscitation protocol.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3126, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-72', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the blood pressure goal for a patient who has both hypertension and diabetes mellitus?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A commonly used older target for patients with hypertension and diabetes was below 130/85 mmHg; current targets may vary according to guideline and individual patient factors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3127, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-73', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse notes an abnormal Q-wave on an ECG but no ST-segment or T-wave changes. How should this be interpreted?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pathologic Q waves without acute ST-T changes can indicate a previous myocardial infarction rather than an acute STEMI.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3128, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-74', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with Aortic Stenosis (AS) reports feeling dizzy and fainting while gardening. What is the primary pathophysiology behind this symptom?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aortic stenosis obstructs left ventricular outflow and limits the increase in cardiac output during exertion, reducing cerebral perfusion and causing syncope.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3129, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-75', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Amina, a 62-year-old patient, is prescribed Pravastatin. What is the standard daily oral dosage range for this medication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pravastatin is commonly administered orally in a daily dose of 10 to 40 mg, depending on the indication and patient factors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3130, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-76', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 55-year-old male abruptly collapses. The monitor reveals an electrophysiological state where the cardiac muscle quivers extremely rapidly without generating any forward stroke volume. This specific incomplete cessation of cardiac pump functioning is clinically defined as:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ventricular fibrillation causes rapid, chaotic ventricular activity that prevents effective cardiac contraction and produces no useful cardiac output.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3131, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-77', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During an assessment of a patient with a suspected aortic dissection, the nurse finds a significant BP difference between arms. Why?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aortic dissection can extend into a branch vessel such as the subclavian artery, producing unequal blood flow and blood pressure between the arms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3132, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-78', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Dr. Bello is considering pharmacological revascularization for a patient with a STEMI. He understands that mortality reduction is highly time-dependent. During which specific phase of treatment is thrombolytic therapy most effective?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thrombolytic therapy is most effective when administered as early as possible after symptom onset because myocardial salvage decreases with time.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3133, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-79', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Peters, a patient suffering from end-stage renal failure, presents with a hypertensive emergency (DBP 150 mm Hg). Despite maximal administration of fast-acting intravenous antihypertensives, his blood pressure remains critically elevated. What is the ultimate, definitive intervention indicated for this specific failure of drug therapy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'In severe hypertension associated with end-stage renal failure that is resistant to medical therapy, dialysis can help remove excess fluid and contribute to blood pressure control.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3134, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-80', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is taking Valsartan OD for hypertension. The nurse knows that this medication is categorized under which functional drug group?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Valsartan is an angiotensin II receptor blocker that selectively blocks the AT1 receptor.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3135, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-81', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient\'s average blood pressure is 160/92 mmHg. According to JNC VI, how is this classified?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Under JNC VI, a systolic pressure of 160 mmHg falls within Stage 2 hypertension, even though the diastolic pressure is lower.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3136, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-82', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which condition is a cause of secondary hypertension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Renal artery stenosis can activate the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system and cause secondary hypertension.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3137, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-83', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why do arteries have more elastic and muscular tissue than veins?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Arteries receive blood directly from the heart under higher pressure, so their elastic and muscular walls help them expand and recoil with each heartbeat.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3138, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-84', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Balogun requires Advanced Life Support (ALS). One of the primary aims of ALS is to \'Reinstate organ perfusion\'. Which of the following is also explicitly listed as an aim of ALS in this protocol?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'ALS aims to restore circulation and organ perfusion and to identify and manage potentially reversible cardiac arrhythmias.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3139, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-85', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which diagnostic test is recommended to determine if a patient has developed left ventricular hypertrophy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Echocardiography can assess left ventricular wall thickness and mass and is more sensitive than ECG for detecting left ventricular hypertrophy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3140, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-86', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Chidi undergoes a successful Primary PCI following a STEMI. Which of the following is a specific listed advantage of Primary PCI when compared directly to thrombolysis in selected patients?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Primary PCI provides more effective mechanical restoration of coronary blood flow and is associated with a lower risk of reocclusion than thrombolytic therapy in appropriate patients.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3141, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-87', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which structure has the thickest wall?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The left ventricle has the thickest muscular wall because it must generate sufficient pressure to pump blood through the systemic circulation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3142, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-88', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is true of the myocardium?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The myocardium is the thick muscular layer of the heart wall. ANP is primarily secreted by atrial cardiomyocytes; this option is the intended answer among the choices.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3143, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-89', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Amina, a 55-year-old diabetic patient, complains of localized chest pain just below her left nipple. She states the pain lasts only a few seconds, feels like a muscle ache, and is easily reproduced when she presses on her chest wall. Based on the triage parameters for chest pain, how should these clinical features be interpreted?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Brief, localized, reproducible chest pain suggests a non-cardiac musculoskeletal cause, but Acute Coronary Syndrome cannot be completely excluded, particularly in a patient with risk factors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3144, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-90', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 48-year-old male complains of chest pain that radiates to his neck and arm. He has a history of syphilis. Which specific etiology should be considered as a potential cause of his angina?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Syphilitic aortitis can damage the aortic root and coronary ostia, potentially causing coronary insufficiency and angina.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3145, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-91', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which non-surgical intervention is used to \'flatten\' plaque against the arterial wall?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Percutaneous transluminal angioplasty uses a balloon to compress or flatten atherosclerotic plaque against the arterial wall and improve blood flow.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3146, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-92', 'mcq', 'medium', 'At which stage in life does thymic atrophy usually begin?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thymic involution begins around puberty, after which the thymus gradually decreases in size and functional tissue.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3147, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-93', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which condition is specifically associated with a hypertensive emergency?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aortic dissection is a life-threatening condition that can present with severe hypertension and acute target-organ injury, making it a hypertensive emergency context.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3148, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-94', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The pulse palpable in the wrist is felt from the:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The radial artery is located at the wrist and is the usual site for palpating the peripheral pulse.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3149, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-95', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient post-saphenous vein stripping reports a \'pins and needles\' sensation in the leg. What does this suggest?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Paresthesia after saphenous vein stripping may indicate irritation or injury to the saphenous nerve, which lies near the vein.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3150, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-96', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Non-Hodgkin lymphomas:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Non-Hodgkin lymphomas are a group of malignant tumors arising from lymphoid tissues and may involve lymph nodes and other organs.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3151, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-97', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Tolu is being evaluated for dyslipidemia. His physician orders an investigation specifically to evaluate the protein components of his lipoproteins. Which test is he ordering?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Apolipoprotein testing measures the protein components of lipoproteins and can help assess cardiovascular risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3152, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-98', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How does Diabetes Mellitus specifically accelerate the atherosclerotic process?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chronic hyperglycemia contributes to vascular injury and thickening of basement membranes, promoting atherosclerotic changes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3153, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-99', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is Troponin I considered superior to CK-MB for diagnosing an MI in a patient who delayed seeking care for 5 days?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Troponin I remains elevated much longer than CK-MB, allowing myocardial injury to be detected several days after the event.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3154, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-100', 'mcq', 'medium', 'People with occupations that involve standing all day are at risk of varicose veins. Why should this be true?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Prolonged standing increases venous hydrostatic pressure in the lower limbs, promoting venous distension and varicosities.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3155, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-101', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 40-year-old male is admitted with a resting blood pressure of 180/110 mm Hg, severe headaches, and blurring of vision. Funduscopic examination reveals papilledema and retinal hemorrhages. Which specific pathological process represents the dominant, destructive vascular hallmark of his current condition?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Malignant hypertension can cause necrotizing arteriolar injury, particularly fibrinoid necrosis of renal arterioles.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3156, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-102', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The sinoatrial node lies:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The sinoatrial node is located in the upper right atrium near the opening of the superior vena cava.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3157, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-103', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During a Code Blue, Dr. Alabi orders Calcium Chloride for a patient in asystole who is not responding to Epinephrine. What is the correct initial IV dose, and when can it be repeated?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'When calcium chloride is specifically indicated during cardiac arrest, a commonly used dose is 10 mL of 10% calcium chloride IV, with repeat dosing guided by the clinical indication and protocol.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3158, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-104', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nurse Bisi is managing a patient who is currently experiencing an acute exacerbation of unstable angina. The physician orders anti-ischemic therapy aiming to produce vasodilation, reduce preload, and reduce myocardial oxygen consumption. Which specific medication and initial administration route fulfills this requirement?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Nitroglycerin given sublingually produces rapid venodilation, reduces preload and myocardial oxygen demand, and can relieve ischemic chest pain.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3159, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-105', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nurse Aisha is performing bag-and-mask ventilation on a patient. She has covered the mouth and nose and connected the oxygen. To ensure a patent airway during this specific procedure, what anatomical adjustment must she make to the patient?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The head-tilt/chin-lift maneuver helps move the tongue away from the posterior pharynx and maintain airway patency when cervical spine injury is not suspected.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3160, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-106', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Danjuma arrives at the A&E complaining of chest pain. His blood pressure is 190/115 mmHg. According to the assessment protocols, which specific examination is particularly useful and indicated given his markedly elevated blood pressure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Funduscopic examination can identify hypertensive retinal changes and evidence of target-organ damage in severe hypertension.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3161, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-107', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What would be a possible consequence of the SA node failing to depolarise?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'If the SA node fails, a slower pacemaker such as the AV node or another subsidiary pacemaker may take over, resulting in a reduced heart rate.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3162, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-108', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Peyer\'s patches are:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Peyer\'s patches are aggregates of lymphoid tissue in the ileum that provide immune surveillance against intestinal antigens.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3163, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-109', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse auscultates a low-pitched rumbling diastolic murmur at the apex of the heart. Which condition does this suggest?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A low-pitched rumbling diastolic murmur best heard at the cardiac apex is characteristic of mitral stenosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3164, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-110', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient, Emeka, collapses suddenly and presents with pallor, cold clammy skin, and pulselessness. He is diagnosed with cardiac arrest. The etiology includes both metabolic and electrophysiological causes. Which of the following is specifically classified as a metabolic etiology for cardiac arrest?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Acidosis is a metabolic cause of cardiac arrest and is included among potentially reversible causes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3165, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-111', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The crash cart arrives for Mr. Eze, who remains in refractory ventricular fibrillation. The physician calls for 200 Joules and presses the charge button on the defibrillator. What is the critical, protocol-mandated action for the resuscitation team members while the machine emits its charging tone?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'CPR should continue while the defibrillator is charging, with everyone clearing the patient immediately before the shock is delivered.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3166, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-112', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse is reviewing the chart of an elderly patient prescribed Digoxin. The patient has a BUN of 45 mg/dL and a Creatinine of 2.8 mg/dL. What does this indicate regarding the Digoxin therapy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Digoxin is primarily eliminated by the kidneys, so impaired renal function can reduce clearance and increase the risk of toxicity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3167, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-113', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following applies to atherosclerosis but not to arteriosclerosis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Atherosclerosis specifically involves the accumulation of lipid-containing plaques in arterial walls, whereas arteriosclerosis is a broader term for arterial stiffening.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3168, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-114', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is reviewing the mechanism of action of Losartan. Losartan lowers blood pressure by selectively blocking Angiotensin II from binding to which receptor?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Losartan is an angiotensin II receptor blocker that selectively antagonizes the AT1 receptor.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3169, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-115', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse is assessing a patient with acute pericarditis. Which finding is considered the hallmark clinical sign of this condition?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A pericardial friction rub is a classic physical finding of acute pericarditis caused by inflamed pericardial layers rubbing together.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3170, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-116', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Kalu, a patient with a history of an old MI, develops a wide-complex tachycardia at a rate of 160 bpm. His QRS duration is 0.16 seconds, and the rhythm is regular. He is complaining of chest pain and feels faint. What is the most effective drug intervention for acute Ventricular Tachycardia (VT) to slow the rate, even if it might not terminate the rhythm?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Amiodarone is an antiarrhythmic commonly used for acute ventricular tachycardia, particularly in patients with structural heart disease.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3171, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-117', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is educating a patient on the mechanism of Cyclandelate. How should the nurse explain its action in managing peripheral vascular symptoms?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cyclandelate is a vasodilator related to papaverine that directly relaxes vascular smooth muscle and increases peripheral blood flow.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3172, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-118', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The visceral pericardium:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The visceral pericardium, also called the epicardium, is the serous membrane directly attached to the surface of the myocardium.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3173, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-119', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient who has been taking Propranolol for chronic angina prophylaxis calls the clinic to say they ran out of pills 3 days ago and feel terrible. The nurse is concerned about which major risk?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Abrupt withdrawal of propranolol can cause rebound sympathetic activity, potentially worsening angina and precipitating myocardial ischemia or infarction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3174, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-120', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient asks if sclerotherapy will \'cure\' their varicose veins. What is the nurse\'s best response?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sclerotherapy closes treated superficial veins and improves symptoms and appearance, but it does not eliminate the underlying tendency to develop varicose veins.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3175, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-121', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient post-cardiac catheterization via the femoral route is instructed to remain on bed rest. What is the primary rationale?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bed rest and maintaining the affected leg in the prescribed position help prevent bleeding from the femoral arterial puncture site.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3176, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-122', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Femi arrives at the emergency unit with acute left ventricular failure, acute pulmonary edema, and a diastolic blood pressure of 145 mm Hg. A junior staff member suggests sublingual administration of fast-acting nifedipine to rapidly lower the pressure. Why must this intervention be avoided?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Immediate-release or sublingual nifedipine can cause an unpredictable and excessive fall in blood pressure, potentially resulting in cerebral or coronary ischemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3177, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-123', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is true of blood vessel diameter?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vascular diameter is strongly influenced by sympathetic autonomic activity, which regulates vascular smooth-muscle contraction and vasoconstriction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3178, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-124', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is taking a fixed low-dose combination of Hydrochlorothiazide and Spironolactone. The nurse knows that Spironolactone is added primarily to:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Spironolactone is potassium-sparing and can help counteract the potassium loss associated with thiazide diuretics.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3179, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-125', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The walls of lymph vessels contain:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lymphatic vessels have an endothelial lining that forms the inner wall and permits lymph to enter; larger lymphatic vessels have additional supporting tissues.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3180, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-126', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with a history of severe hepatic cirrhosis is prescribed Telmisartan for hypertension. What modification should the nurse anticipate?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Telmisartan is extensively metabolized in the liver, and its use requires caution and dose limitation in patients with hepatic impairment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3181, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-127', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 60-year-old male, Femi, presents to the emergency room unconscious. The team must determine if the collapse is due to cardiac arrest. According to the Initial Response protocol, which three vital parameters must be immediately observed?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Initial recognition of cardiac arrest includes rapidly assessing breathing, skin color, and pulse while initiating the emergency response.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3182, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-128', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Some capillaries are called sinusoids. These are capillaries that:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sinusoidal capillaries have a discontinuous endothelium with large gaps, allowing passage of larger molecules and sometimes cells.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3183, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-129', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 65-year-old female, Mrs. Tolu, presents with an Acute Myocardial Infarction. Her ECG shows abnormal Q waves, but no ST-segment elevation or loss of R-wave progression in the anterior leads. Instead, ST-segment and T-wave changes are noted in other appropriate leads. These specific ECG findings are most consistent with an infarction in which myocardial region?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Posterior myocardial infarction may produce reciprocal ST-T changes and Q-wave patterns in the appropriate leads rather than the typical anterior-lead findings.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3184, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-130', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which blood vessel links the gastrointestinal tract and the liver?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The hepatic portal vein carries nutrient-rich blood from the gastrointestinal tract to the liver for processing.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3185, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-131', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is the myocardium of the right ventricle thinner than that of the left ventricle?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The right ventricle pumps blood into the lower-resistance pulmonary circulation and therefore requires less muscular force than the left ventricle.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3186, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-132', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why does the lumen of a large vein have a larger diameter than the lumen of a large artery?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Veins are capacitance vessels that contain most of the body\'s blood volume and therefore have relatively large lumens.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3187, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-133', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nurse Blessing is preparing to administer Atropine to a patient in asystole. What is the specific dosage indicated for this condition in the provided protocol?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The older protocol referenced uses atropine 3 mg IV for asystole; however, current adult cardiac arrest guidelines do not routinely recommend atropine for asystole or PEA.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3188, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-134', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Cardiac muscle cells differ from skeletal muscle cells in that:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cardiac muscle is involuntary, whereas skeletal muscle is under voluntary control.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3189, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-135', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In the pharmacological management of an asystolic arrest, three specific medications are explicitly listed after continuing CPR and ruling out the use of an external shock. Which combination correctly identifies these three critical drugs?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'According to the older protocol referenced by the question, epinephrine, atropine, and calcium chloride were listed for asystolic arrest; current guidelines primarily recommend epinephrine and treatment of reversible causes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3190, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-136', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which period of the heart cycle is completely occupied by the ventricles contracting?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ventricular systole is the phase of the cardiac cycle during which the ventricles contract and eject blood.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3191, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-137', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Dobutamine increases contractility but carries a risk of:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dobutamine stimulates beta-1 receptors and increases contractility but may also increase heart rate and precipitate tachydysrhythmias.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3192, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-138', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Aisha is diagnosed with secondary hypertension. A comprehensive renal ultrasound and pyelography are ordered to identify the exact etiology. Which of the following conditions represents a structural renal disorder known to directly cause this type of hypertension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Polycystic kidney disease is a structural renal disorder that can cause secondary hypertension through renal vascular and hormonal mechanisms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3193, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-139', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which medication is added to the treatment plan for NYHA Class III and IV heart failure to reduce mortality?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Spironolactone, a mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist, has been shown to reduce morbidity and mortality in selected patients with symptomatic heart failure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3194, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-140', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient presents with acute bacterial endocarditis. The physician orders a massive dose of intravenous antibiotics to control the infection. If Ampicillin is chosen as the drug of choice, what is the prescribed intensive IV dosage regimen during the acute phase?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'High-dose intravenous ampicillin may be used in selected cases of enterococcal endocarditis, with dosing divided throughout the day during intensive therapy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3195, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-141', 'mcq', 'medium', 'An elderly patient prescribed nifedipine for hypertension complains of a burning sensation in the chest after meals. The nurse recognizes this as a potential worsening of which condition associated with this medication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Nifedipine can relax the lower esophageal sphincter and may worsen gastroesophageal reflux symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3196, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-142', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Dr. Eze is conducting a rural health screening and suspects a patient has primary hypertension. To establish a definitive, protocol-driven clinical diagnosis, what exact blood pressure thresholds and recording frequency must be documented?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The question\'s provided protocol identifies repeated measurements above 140/100 mmHg over several days; diagnostic thresholds vary among guidelines, so local protocol should be followed.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3197, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-143', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During continuous ECG monitoring, why is Lead II frequently selected?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lead II is commonly used for rhythm monitoring because the electrical axis often provides a clear view of atrial activity and the P waves.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3198, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-144', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Verapamil lowers cardiac workload and treats arrhythmias by exerting which specific effects on the heart?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Verapamil blocks L-type calcium channels, producing negative chronotropic and negative inotropic effects and slowing AV nodal conduction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3199, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-145', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is admitted with acute pulmonary edema secondary to acute hypertensive crisis. The physician orders Reserpine 1?2 mg IM, to be repeated 12 hourly. What adverse effect should the nursing staff monitor for?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Reserpine can cause significant hypotension because it depletes catecholamines and reduces sympathetic activity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3200, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-146', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Chukwu, a 60-year-old smoker, experiences squeezing retrosternal chest pain after walking up a flight of stairs. The pain resolves after he sits down for five minutes. This presentation is most characteristic of which condition?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Stable angina typically occurs with exertion and is relieved by rest.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3201, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-147', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Chidi has a severe headache and BP of 190/145 mmHg. What distinguishes hypertensive emergency from hypertensive urgency?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hypertensive emergency is defined by severe BP elevation accompanied by acute target-organ damage.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3202, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-148', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 50-year-old male develops atrial flutter following mitral valve surgery. His ventricular rate is poorly controlled and DC cardioversion is planned. What is the recommended top choice energy level?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Atrial flutter is usually highly responsive to synchronized cardioversion, often with a relatively low energy such as 25?50 J.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3203, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-149', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What will cause the sinoatrial node to depolarize more frequently?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Norepinephrine stimulates beta-1 receptors in the SA node, increasing the rate of pacemaker depolarization.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3204, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-150', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the priority nursing intervention for a patient with valvular disease and new-onset hemoptysis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'New hemoptysis may indicate pulmonary congestion or other serious complications and requires prompt assessment and notification.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3205, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-151', 'mcq', 'medium', 'When listening to the lub-dup sound of the heart, what causes the \'dup\' sound?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'S2 is produced mainly by closure and vibration associated with the aortic and pulmonary semilunar valves.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3206, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-152', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with aortic stenosis has a loud rough systolic crescendo-decrescendo murmur. Where is a palpable thrill most likely felt?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aortic stenosis produces a systolic thrill best felt at the aortic area at the base of the heart.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3207, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-153', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Alabi has sustained ventricular tachycardia without a palpable pulse. What is the sequential energy escalation protocol for the initial three shocks?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The question reflects an older escalating-energy protocol. Current defibrillation energy depends on the defibrillator and manufacturer recommendations.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3208, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-154', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Yusuf requires immediate pain relief for suspected acute myocardial infarction. Which analgesic is given IV at 50?100 mg and generally causes less nausea and vomiting than morphine?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pethidine has historically been used as an opioid alternative and may cause less nausea and vomiting than morphine.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3209, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-155', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which valvular disorder is most closely associated with rheumatic endocarditis causing leaflet fusion?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rheumatic heart disease commonly causes commissural fusion and thickening of the mitral valve, producing mitral stenosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3210, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-156', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During cardiovascular examination, where is the aortic stenosis murmur best auscultated?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aortic stenosis is best heard at the right second intercostal space and typically radiates toward the carotids.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3211, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-157', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with acute chest pain receives IV access, ECG monitoring, oxygen, and morphine 4 mg IV. When should morphine be considered?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Morphine is generally reserved for severe persistent pain despite appropriate anti-ischemic treatment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3212, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-158', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A ventricular aneurysm increases the risk of which potentially fatal event?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A ventricular aneurysm is associated with complications such as ventricular arrhythmias, thromboembolism, and, depending on the type, risk of rupture.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3213, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-159', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient in Phase II cardiac rehabilitation develops chest pain and palpitations during exercise. What should the nurse instruct?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chest pain and palpitations during exercise may indicate myocardial ischemia or dysrhythmia, so exercise should be stopped immediately.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3214, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-160', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which medication is preferred for pharmacologic stress testing in a patient with severe asthma or bronchospasm?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Adenosine and dipyridamole can provoke bronchospasm; dobutamine is generally preferred when vasodilator agents are unsuitable.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3215, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-161', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Fusion of semilunar leaflets causes a marked increase in left ventricular pressure. Which pathological state ultimately results?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe aortic stenosis increases left ventricular afterload and can progress to left ventricular failure and reduced cardiac output.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3216, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-162', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which capillaries allow cells and plasma proteins to enter or leave their lumen?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sinusoidal capillaries have large gaps and a discontinuous basement membrane, allowing cells and large proteins to pass.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3217, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-163', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which medication is a preferred IV vasodilator for initial treatment of a hypertensive emergency?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sodium nitroprusside is a potent IV vasodilator that can rapidly and controllably reduce blood pressure in selected hypertensive emergencies.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3218, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-164', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient has chest pain, dyspnea, and ST-segment elevation. Which condition is an important differential diagnosis for STEMI?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Acute pericarditis can produce ST-segment elevation and must be distinguished from acute myocardial infarction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3219, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-165', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Labetalol is unique among sympatholytics because it reduces blood pressure through what mechanism?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Labetalol blocks both alpha-1 and beta adrenergic receptors, reducing vascular resistance and cardiac sympathetic effects.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3220, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-166', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which factor is a hypothesized cause of multifactorial hypertension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Increased renal sodium retention can expand extracellular fluid volume and contribute to increased blood pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3221, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-167', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mrs. Hassan has persistent ventricular tachycardia. What is the correct continuous IV infusion rate of lignocaine following an initial 1.5 mg/kg bolus?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'After an IV lidocaine/lignocaine bolus, the usual maintenance infusion is approximately 1?4 mg/min; 2?4 mg/min matches the option provided.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3222, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-168', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is the short half-life of adenosine beneficial during a pharmacologic stress test?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Adenosine is rapidly cleared, so adverse effects generally resolve quickly when the infusion is discontinued.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3223, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-169', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A stable patient has regular wide-complex tachycardia after a prior MI. Which pacing method can terminate the rhythm if drugs are ineffective or not preferred?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Anti-tachycardia pacing can terminate certain reentrant ventricular tachycardias by pacing the circuit faster than the tachycardia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(3224, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-170', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A symptomatic patient with aortic stenosis is not a surgical candidate. Which procedure might be used as a bridge or palliative measure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Balloon aortic valvuloplasty can provide temporary symptomatic or hemodynamic improvement in selected patients who cannot undergo definitive valve replacement.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3225, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-171', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which laboratory value is most critical to monitor in a patient taking furosemide?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Furosemide can cause significant potassium loss, making serum potassium monitoring important.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3226, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-172', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Chidi has pre-existing SA block and heart failure. Which calcium channel blocker is contraindicated?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Verapamil depresses SA/AV nodal conduction and myocardial contractility and is contraindicated in significant conduction disease and certain forms of heart failure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3227, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-173', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is prescribed propranolol. Which condition in the patient\'s medical history would prompt the nurse to immediately question the order?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Propranolol is a nonselective beta-blocker that can cause bronchoconstriction and should be used cautiously or avoided in severe obstructive airway disease.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3228, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-174', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is being evaluated for heart failure. Which laboratory test is specifically used as a biomarker for ventricular stretch and pressure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'BNP is released by ventricular myocardium in response to increased ventricular wall stretch and pressure and is useful in evaluating heart failure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3229, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-175', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 45-year-old female, Zainab, is newly diagnosed with mild hypertension and has no other coexisting medical conditions. Based on the selective drug therapy protocol for a patient under age 50, which class is designated as the primary first-line option?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'In the age-based protocol reflected by the question, ACE inhibitors or ARBs are selected first-line for younger patients without specific contraindications.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3230, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-176', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which statement accurately contrasts Captopril and Enalapril?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Captopril absorption can be reduced by food, so it is generally taken before meals. Enalapril may be taken with or without food.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3231, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-177', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The superior sagittal sinus drains blood from the superior part of the brain directly into:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The superior sagittal sinus drains posteriorly into the confluence of sinuses, which then communicates with the transverse sinuses.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3232, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-178', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A PET scan of the heart shows an area with significantly decreased blood flow but high glucose metabolism. What does this indicate?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Reduced perfusion with preserved glucose metabolism indicates viable but ischemic myocardium, often described as hibernating myocardium.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3233, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-179', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient reports highly erratic blood pressure readings since starting valsartan and takes the drug sometimes with breakfast and sometimes on an empty stomach. What is the pharmacological rationale?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Food can reduce valsartan exposure and bioavailability. Consistent administration in relation to meals helps maintain more predictable drug exposure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3234, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-180', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What feature does cardiac muscle possess that is missing in skeletal muscle?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Intercalated discs connect cardiac muscle cells and facilitate coordinated electrical and mechanical activity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3235, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-181', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which important vein is formed by the union of the right and left brachiocephalic veins?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The right and left brachiocephalic veins unite to form the superior vena cava.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3236, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-182', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is nesiritide (Natrecor) used in decompensated heart failure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Nesiritide is a recombinant B-type natriuretic peptide that promotes vasodilation and natriuresis and counteracts maladaptive neurohormonal activity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3237, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-183', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which assessment finding suggests the MI has progressed to heart failure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pulmonary crackles and jugular venous distension indicate fluid congestion and elevated cardiac filling pressures associated with heart failure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3238, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-184', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In adult CPR, what is the treatment of choice for ventricular fibrillation?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Ventricular fibrillation is a shockable cardiac arrest rhythm; immediate unsynchronized defibrillation combined with high-quality CPR is indicated.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3239, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-185', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following does NOT assist in returning blood to the heart through veins?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Gravity generally opposes venous return from the lower extremities when a person is upright, whereas venous valves and the respiratory and muscle pumps assist return.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3240, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-186', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient has failed initial single-drug therapy for hypertension. Which is NOT a primary reason for utilizing low-dose combination therapy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Combination therapy is used to improve BP control and may allow lower doses that reduce adverse effects; intentionally causing postural hypotension is not a therapeutic goal.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3241, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-187', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient receiving a loop diuretic is at high risk for hypokalemia. Which potassium-sparing adjunct and dosing regimen is specified?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Spironolactone (Aldactone) is potassium-sparing; 25 mg once daily is a commonly used low starting dose, depending on the clinical indication and patient factors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3242, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-188', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 12-year-old boy develops fever, flitting polyarthritis, and purposeless jerky movements of the face and limbs. Which dermatological manifestation is most likely?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The presentation is consistent with acute rheumatic fever with Sydenham chorea. Erythema marginatum is a characteristic associated skin manifestation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3243, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-189', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which assessment finding indicates that magnesium sulfate therapy for an arrhythmia is becoming toxic?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Magnesium toxicity causes neuromuscular depression, beginning with diminished or absent deep tendon reflexes and potentially progressing to respiratory depression.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3244, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-190', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with severe digoxin toxicity suddenly develops a dangerous ventricular arrhythmia. Which emergency medication should the nurse prepare to administer?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lidocaine can be used to treat certain ventricular dysrhythmias associated with digoxin toxicity; severe toxicity may also require digoxin-specific antibody fragments.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3245, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-191', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient asks when it is safe to resume sexual activity after an MI. What is the standard guideline?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Resumption of sexual activity is generally considered when the patient can perform moderate physical activity without angina, excessive dyspnea, or other significant symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3246, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-192', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A bystander initiates first aid by lifting the chin and tilting the head backwards. What is the primary anatomical purpose of these airway maneuvers?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Head tilt?chin lift moves the tongue away from the posterior pharyngeal wall and helps open the airway in an unresponsive patient without suspected cervical spine injury.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3247, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-193', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Why is lidocaine not administered orally for the treatment of ventricular arrhythmias?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Oral lidocaine undergoes extensive hepatic first-pass metabolism, resulting in very low systemic bioavailability and making it unsuitable for systemic antiarrhythmic therapy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3248, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-194', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which physiological mechanism explains why a heavy meal can precipitate an anginal attack?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Digestion increases metabolic demand and splanchnic blood flow; in patients with limited coronary reserve, the increased cardiovascular demand can precipitate ischemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3249, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-195', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The pulmonary circulation:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pulmonary circulation is a low-pressure, low-resistance circuit. The right ventricle pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs through the pulmonary artery.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3250, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-196', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Where are the baroreceptors controlling blood pressure located?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Arterial baroreceptors are located primarily in the carotid sinus and aortic arch and detect changes in arterial pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3251, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-197', 'mcq', 'medium', 'According to the JNC VI guidelines, what defines Stage 3 hypertension?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Under JNC VI, Stage 3 hypertension was defined as systolic pressure ?180 mmHg or diastolic pressure ?110 mmHg.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3252, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-198', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Given blood pressure of 28 mmHg and osmotic pressure of 20 mmHg at the arterial end of a capillary, what is the net filtration pressure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Using the simplified relationship, net filtration pressure = hydrostatic pressure ? osmotic pressure = 28 ? 20 = 8 mmHg.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3253, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-199', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with mitral valve prolapse reports frequent palpitations and anxiety. Which lifestyle modification should the nurse prioritize?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Caffeine and alcohol can increase palpitations in susceptible patients, so limiting or avoiding them may reduce symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3254, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-200', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mr. Hassan, 65, has dyspnea, orthopnea, weakness, engorged neck veins, and pulmonary congestion two weeks after an MI. What complication of AMI do these findings most strongly indicate?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dyspnea, orthopnea, pulmonary congestion, and jugular venous distension are classic findings of heart failure following myocardial infarction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3255, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-201', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following statements best describes the safety profile of cardiac glycosides like Digoxin?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Digoxin has a narrow therapeutic index, meaning there is a relatively small difference between therapeutic and toxic concentrations. Patients require careful monitoring for toxicity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3256, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-202', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 45-year-old patient with an acute myocardial infarction develops Ventricular Fibrillation (VF). The resuscitation team immediately initiates CPR and prepares for defibrillation. According to the specific shock cycles outlined, what is the correct energy sequence for the initial group of three shocks if the VF persists?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The intended sequence in the question is 200 J, 200 J, then 360 J. Defibrillation energy recommendations depend on whether a monophasic or biphasic defibrillator is being used.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3257, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-203', 'mcq', 'medium', 'What is the clinical significance of a patient\'s angina changing from \'stable\' to \'unstable\'?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Unstable angina is associated with plaque disruption and increased coronary thrombosis risk. It is an acute coronary syndrome and may precede myocardial infarction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3258, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-204', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient in hypertensive urgency is being treated with oral agents. Which class does Clonidine belong to?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Clonidine is a centrally acting alpha-2 adrenergic agonist. It reduces sympathetic outflow from the central nervous system and lowers blood pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3259, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-205', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse reviews the medication list of a patient with peripheral vascular disease and notes: Aspirin, Clopidogrel, and Vitamin E. What is the cumulative pharmacological effect of this specific combination?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aspirin and clopidogrel inhibit platelet aggregation, while vitamin E may also increase bleeding tendency. Together, the combination may increase protection against arterial thrombosis but also increases bleeding risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3260, 9, 34, NULL, 'AB-DEV-206', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The tricuspid valve separates which two structures?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The tricuspid valve lies between the right atrium and right ventricle and prevents backflow of blood into the right atrium during ventricular systole.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:03:00', '2026-10-10 15:03:00', NULL),
(3263, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-03', 'mcq', 'hard', 'What is the primary site of oxygen and nutrient exchange in the fetus?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The placenta is the organ where oxygen, nutrients, and waste products are exchanged between the mother and fetus.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3264, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-04', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The best time to suction the airway of a convulsing patient is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Suctioning during a seizure can cause injury and aspiration; airway suctioning is safest after the seizure when necessary.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3265, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-05', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The First Republic of Nigeria was brought to an end by a military coup on', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The First Republic ended following the military coup of 15 January 1966.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3266, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-06', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A client is being discharged on warfarin for atrial fibrillation. The nurse must teach the client that which over-the-counter medication is contraindicated?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Aspirin increases bleeding risk when combined with warfarin.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3267, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-07', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The activated fatty acid is transported across the inner mitochondrial membrane using a shuttle system called the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The carnitine shuttle transports long-chain fatty acids into the mitochondrial matrix for beta-oxidation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3268, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-08', 'mcq', 'hard', 'An opening in the diaphragm called the __________ hiatus allows the esophagus to pass through to the stomach', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The esophageal hiatus is the opening through which the esophagus passes through the diaphragm.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3269, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-09', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The greatest immediate danger to a woman with postpartum psychosis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Postpartum psychosis can cause severe loss of judgment and may result in suicide or harm to the infant.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3270, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-10', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which complication does Z-track technique primarily prevent?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The Z-track technique prevents medication from leaking back into subcutaneous tissue.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3271, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-11', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A patient who has a strong emotional outburst and then has no memory of the event is likely using what defense mechanism', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Repression involves unconsciously blocking distressing thoughts or experiences from conscious awareness.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3272, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-12', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The rationale for recommending stool softeners to a woman with a repaired episiotomy is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Stool softeners reduce straining, which helps protect the healing perineal wound.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3273, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-13', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In a face presentation, the presenting diameter is the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The submentobregmatic diameter is the presenting anteroposterior diameter in a face presentation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3274, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-14', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A patient asks about PEP duration. Post-exposure prophylaxis is taken for which duration to be effective?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'HIV post-exposure prophylaxis is generally taken for 28 days.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3275, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-15', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Menopause is physiologically defined by the depletion of ovarian follicles, leading to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Declining estrogen production causes loss of negative feedback, resulting in elevated FSH levels.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3276, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-16', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A hydrocolloid dressing is most appropriate for a wound that is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hydrocolloid dressings are suitable for clean wounds with low to moderate exudate.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3277, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-17', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which of the following is the most common type of dementia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Alzheimer\'s disease is the most common form of dementia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3278, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-18', 'mcq', 'hard', 'All of the following are direct methods of nutritional assessment EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Clinical examination, anthropometry and biochemical tests directly assess nutritional status; vital statistics do not.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3279, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-19', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The hallmark clinical sign of kwashiorkor is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Oedema is a characteristic clinical feature of kwashiorkor.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3280, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-20', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In the fetal skull, the suture between the two halves of the forehead bone, which usually fuses in early infancy, is the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The frontal or metopic suture lies between the two frontal bones.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3281, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-21', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Folic acid supplementation before and during early pregnancy reduces the risk of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Folic acid reduces the risk of fetal neural tube defects such as spina bifida.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3282, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-22', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The following data show the number of hours worked by 200 statistics students. What is the class width for this distribution? Number of Hours | Frequency 0 - 9 | 40 10 - 19 | 50 20 - 29 | 70 30 - 39 | 40', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Class width is the difference between consecutive lower class limits, which is 10.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3283, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-23', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A positive Ortolani or Barlow maneuver in a newborn suggests', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Positive Ortolani or Barlow maneuvers indicate instability associated with developmental dysplasia of the hip.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3284, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-24', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A woman with polyhydramnios is at risk of which complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Excessive amniotic fluid increases the likelihood of cord prolapse, especially after rupture of membranes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3285, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-25', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In which year were the Northern and Southern protectorates merged to form the colony and protectorate of Nigeria?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The Northern and Southern Protectorates were amalgamated in 1914.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3286, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-26', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which type of study design allows researchers to infer cause and effect most strongly?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Experimental studies, especially randomized controlled trials, provide the strongest evidence for causal relationships.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3287, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-27', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which of the following is a life-threatening complication of severe preeclampsia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe hypertension in preeclampsia can cause cerebral haemorrhage, seizures and other serious neurological complications.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3288, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-28', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In managing shoulder dystocia, the McRoberts manoeuvre involves', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The McRoberts manoeuvre involves hyperflexing the mother\'s thighs onto her abdomen to help release the impacted shoulder.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3289, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-29', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A patient with respiratory acidosis has CO2 retention. The underlying problem in respiratory acidosis is which physiological issue?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hypoventilation causes inadequate removal of carbon dioxide, resulting in respiratory acidosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3290, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-30', 'mcq', 'hard', 'When a pregnant woman lies on her back for a long period, she might develop????????????', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The gravid uterus can compress the inferior vena cava when the woman lies supine, reducing venous return and causing supine hypotension.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3291, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-31', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Nigeria formally became a federation under the constitution of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The 1954 Constitution established Nigeria as a federation with greater regional autonomy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3292, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-32', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A patient asks about malaria in travelers versus endemic residents. Travelers are more likely to develop severe malaria because of which factor?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'People from non-endemic areas generally lack the partial immunity acquired through repeated exposure to malaria.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3293, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-33', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Health education at primary health care level is most effective when it', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Community participation improves relevance, understanding, acceptance and sustainability of health education.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3294, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-34', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A newborn develops tremors and irritability after birth from a diabetic mother. This is commonly due to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Infants of diabetic mothers are at increased risk of neonatal hypoglycaemia, which can cause tremors and irritability.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3295, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-35', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Electroencephalography is mainly used to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'EEG records the electrical activity of the brain and is useful in assessing conditions such as epilepsy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3296, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-36', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which is a danger sign in pregnancy requiring immediate care?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vaginal bleeding during pregnancy may indicate a serious complication and requires prompt assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3297, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-37', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which nursing activity best describes health promotion?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Health promotion involves helping individuals adopt behaviours that improve and maintain health.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3298, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-38', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In email, BCC is used to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'BCC allows recipients to receive an email without their addresses being visible to other recipients.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3299, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-39', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A key sign of uterine rupture during labour is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe, persistent abdominal pain may occur with uterine rupture and requires immediate intervention.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3300, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-40', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Furosemide acts mainly on the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Furosemide is a loop diuretic that inhibits sodium and chloride reabsorption in the thick ascending limb of the loop of Henle.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3301, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-41', 'mcq', 'hard', 'For a patient with hepatic encephalopathy, the most appropriate general dietary plan is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Patients with hepatic encephalopathy generally need adequate energy and protein; routine severe protein restriction is not recommended.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3302, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-42', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Colloid osmotic pressure is the osmotic pressure exerted mainly by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Plasma proteins, especially albumin, are primarily responsible for colloid osmotic pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3303, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-43', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A nurse is caring for a client with active, laryngeal tuberculosis in the hospital. The most appropriate type of isolation precaution is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Active tuberculosis is transmitted through airborne particles, so airborne precautions are required.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3304, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-44', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In supine hypotensive syndrome, the gravid uterus compresses the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The enlarged uterus can compress the inferior vena cava when the pregnant woman lies supine, reducing venous return.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3305, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-45', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A client with unexplained vaginal bleeding should defer which method until evaluated', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Unexplained vaginal bleeding should be assessed before insertion of an IUCD.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3306, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-46', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A fracture at the base of the first metacarpal affecting thumb movement is BEST described as a', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A Bennett fracture is an intra-articular fracture at the base of the first metacarpal.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3307, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-47', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which of the following is a function of the respiratory system?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The respiratory system performs gas exchange, taking in oxygen and eliminating carbon dioxide.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3308, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-48', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Colour vision is mediated by which retinal cells?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cone cells are responsible for colour vision and detailed vision in bright light.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3309, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-49', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which form of written communication always carries a subject line?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Memos commonly contain a subject line that identifies the purpose or topic of the communication.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3310, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-50', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A woman in labour with breech presentation is at risk of which complication?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Breech presentation increases the risk of umbilical cord prolapse, particularly after rupture of the membranes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3311, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-51', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which evaluation type measures long-term program impact?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Summative evaluation assesses the overall outcomes and impact of a programme after implementation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3312, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-52', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A patient on thiazide diuretic develops hyponatremia. Thiazides impair dilution by blocking sodium reabsorption in which nephron segment?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thiazides inhibit sodium and chloride reabsorption in the distal convoluted tubule, impairing urine dilution.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3313, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-53', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which capacity does community resilience primarily describe?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Community resilience refers to the ability of a community to withstand, adapt to and recover from adversity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3314, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-54', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The rationale for advising a constipated pregnant client to increase fluid intake is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Adequate fluid intake helps soften stools and makes bowel movements easier.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3315, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-55', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which diuretic can cause ototoxicity if given too fast IV?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rapid intravenous administration of furosemide can cause ototoxicity, particularly at high doses.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3316, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-56', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which pathway do inhaled corticosteroids primarily prevent exacerbations through?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Inhaled corticosteroids reduce airway inflammation, thereby decreasing asthma exacerbations.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3317, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-57', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A client with a newly applied plaster cast on their leg complains of intense pain unrelieved by analgesics. The nurse\'s priority action is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Severe pain unrelieved by analgesics may indicate impaired circulation or compartment syndrome, so immediate neurovascular assessment is essential.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3318, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-58', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which of these cardiovascular changes occur in pregnancy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pregnancy causes an increase in plasma volume that produces physiological haemodilution.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3319, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-59', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Peptic ulcer disease most commonly affects the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Peptic ulcers most commonly occur in the stomach and duodenum.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3320, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-60', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A woman with severe pre-eclampsia develops right upper quadrant pain. This most likely indicates', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Right upper quadrant or epigastric pain in severe pre-eclampsia may indicate hepatic involvement and possible HELLP syndrome.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3321, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-61', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Calcium channel blockers relieve angina mainly by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Calcium channel blockers reduce coronary vascular resistance and dilate peripheral arteries, improving myocardial oxygen supply and reducing workload.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3322, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-62', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The part of the sclera perforated for passage of optic nerve fibres is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The lamina cribrosa is the perforated portion of the sclera through which optic nerve fibres pass.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3323, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-63', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The primary goal of medical treatment for endometriosis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The main immediate goal of medical treatment for endometriosis is relief of pain and suppression of symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3324, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-64', 'mcq', 'hard', 'An early symptom of strangulation in bilateral inguinal hernia is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sharp abdominal pain is an early warning sign of strangulation and requires urgent assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3325, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-65', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A mother brings her infant with severe diarrhoea to the clinic. The nurse notes the infant has sunken fontanelles, tachycardia, and is unable to drink. The priority nursing action is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The infant has signs of severe dehydration and is unable to drink, making urgent intravenous rehydration the priority.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3326, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-66', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A woman at 14 weeks\' gestation has no documented tetanus-containing vaccine doses and needs catch-up Td vaccination. What is the appropriate response?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tetanus-containing vaccination can be given during pregnancy when indicated; vaccination should not be unnecessarily delayed.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3327, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-67', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A mother worries that her breast milk looks thin and watery at the start of a feed. The midwife should explain that this milk is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Foremilk is the milk available at the beginning of a feed and generally appears thinner and more watery than hindmilk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3328, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-68', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A client with acute decompensated heart failure is receiving an IV infusion of dobutamine. The nurse expects this medication to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Dobutamine is an inotropic medication that increases myocardial contractility and cardiac output.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3329, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-69', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Emotional intelligence is the ability to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Emotional intelligence involves recognising, understanding and managing one\'s own emotions and those of others.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3330, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-70', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A patient taking acetaminophen exceeds the maximum daily dose. The major toxicity concern with acetaminophen overdose is which organ damage?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Excessive acetaminophen can cause severe liver injury and potentially acute hepatic failure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3331, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-71', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The internal pudendal artery arises directly from which parent vessel?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The internal pudendal artery usually arises from the anterior division of the internal iliac artery.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3332, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-72', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The ascending colon is supplied mainly by branches of the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The ascending colon receives its main arterial supply from branches of the superior mesenteric artery.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3333, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-73', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Penicillins and cephalosporins, which are considered safe in pregnancy, act by inhibiting bacterial', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Beta-lactam antibiotics inhibit bacterial cell wall synthesis by binding to penicillin-binding proteins.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3334, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-74', 'mcq', 'hard', 'At primary health care level, oral rehydration solution is primarily used to treat', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'ORS replaces water and electrolytes lost through diarrhoea and is a key treatment for dehydration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3335, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-75', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Orange discoloration of urine and tears is a harmless side effect of which anti-TB drug?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rifampicin commonly causes harmless orange-red discoloration of urine, tears and other body fluids.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3336, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-76', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The ethical principle of truth telling is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Veracity is the ethical principle requiring healthcare professionals to tell the truth.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3337, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-77', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The normal respiratory rate for an adult at rest is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A normal resting respiratory rate for an adult is generally 12-20 breaths per minute.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3338, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-78', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Disappearance of the Moro and rooting reflexes at the expected age indicates', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The normal disappearance of primitive reflexes reflects maturation of the central nervous system.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3339, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-79', 'mcq', 'hard', '0.25 L equals', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'One litre equals 1,000 mL, so 0.25 L equals 250 mL.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3340, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-80', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The intertragal notch of the pinna lies between the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The intertragal notch is the depression between the tragus and antitragus.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3341, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-81', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A vague feeling of discomfort or dread whose source is unknown is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Anxiety is a vague feeling of apprehension or dread that may occur without an identifiable source.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3342, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-82', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which of the following is a primary (first-line) defence against infection?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Intact skin forms a physical barrier that prevents many pathogens from entering the body.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3343, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-83', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The narrow fibrous joints between the bones of the fetal skull are called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sutures are fibrous joints between the bones of the fetal skull and allow limited movement during birth.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3344, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-84', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Drug resistance in tuberculosis management is due to...', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'TB drug resistance commonly develops through spontaneous genetic mutations that confer resistance to specific drugs.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3345, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-85', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Amiodarone contains a high proportion of which element?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Amiodarone contains a high iodine content, which can affect thyroid function.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3346, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-86', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Sperm is produced in which structure within the testes?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Spermatogenesis occurs within the seminiferous tubules of the testes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3347, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-87', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The most serious adverse effect associated with metformin is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Although rare, lactic acidosis is the most serious adverse effect associated with metformin.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3348, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-88', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A patient with chronic gout receives allopurinol for prophylaxis. Urate-lowering therapy prevents flares by maintaining uric acid below which level?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'For most patients with gout, serum urate is targeted below 6 mg/dL to reduce crystal deposition and prevent flares.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3349, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-89', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The most inferior part of the brain stem is known as the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The medulla oblongata is the lowest part of the brainstem and connects with the spinal cord.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3350, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-90', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The transparent anterior part of the outer fibrous coat of the eye is the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The cornea is the transparent anterior portion of the eye\'s outer fibrous coat.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3351, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-91', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which is the normal fetal presentation at term?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cephalic presentation, with the fetal head presenting first, is the normal presentation at term.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3352, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-92', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which is a modifiable risk factor for stroke?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Elevated blood pressure is a major modifiable risk factor for stroke and should be appropriately controlled.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3353, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-93', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Incongruity of affect is best described as', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Incongruent affect occurs when the emotional expression does not match the content or situation, such as laughing while discussing a painful event.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3354, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-94', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The pineal gland is located in the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The pineal gland is a small endocrine gland located in the epithalamus of the brain.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3355, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-95', 'mcq', 'hard', 'An infusion of 500 mL is to run over 4 hours using a giving set calibrated at 15 gtt/mL. The rate in drops per minute is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Using the formula (500 ? 15) ? (4 ? 60), the rate is approximately 31 drops per minute.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3356, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-96', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A primary health care worker\'s main role in the community is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Primary health care emphasizes health promotion, disease prevention, community participation and appropriate care.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3357, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-97', 'mcq', 'hard', 'An elderly patient with multiple comorbidities needs pain management. Opioid dosing in elderly should be adjusted by starting with which approach?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Elderly patients are more sensitive to opioids and may have reduced drug clearance, so treatment should start at a lower dose.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3358, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-98', 'mcq', 'hard', 'What is the term for a type of summary writing that restricts the writer to specific instructions based on words, sentences, or paragraphs?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Guided summary requires the writer to follow specified instructions or limits concerning the content and form of the summary.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3359, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-99', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Erythroplakia appears as a', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Erythroplakia is characterized clinically by a red, velvety mucosal patch.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(3360, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-100', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which of the following vital centres is NOT present in the Medulla oblongata?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The hypothalamus contains regulatory centres, whereas the medulla contains important cardiovascular and respiratory centres.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3361, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-101', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Relaxation of the rib cage ligaments in pregnancy results in', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pregnancy causes relaxation of the thoracic ligaments and increases the transverse and anteroposterior dimensions of the chest.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3362, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-102', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In a malaria case management training programme, quality improvement aims to ensure health workers treat patients according to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Quality improvement promotes adherence to evidence-based national treatment guidelines.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3363, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-103', 'mcq', 'hard', 'According to WHO, a child under 5 years with BMI-for-age above +3 SD is classified as', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A BMI-for-age above +3 standard deviations in children under five is classified as obesity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3364, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-104', 'mcq', 'hard', 'An older adult with a serious infection is most likely to present with', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Older adults may have atypical infection presentations, with acute confusion or delirium being an important warning sign.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3365, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-105', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Diffuse enlargement of the thyroid gland due to hyperplasia is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Goitre refers to enlargement of the thyroid gland, which may result from hyperplasia or other causes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3366, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-106', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A key social-emotional milestone in a nine-month-old is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Stranger anxiety commonly develops during late infancy and reflects attachment and cognitive development.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3367, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-107', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A patient with eating disorder is started on nutrition. Thiamine supplementation in refeeding prevents which neurological condition?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thiamine supplementation during refeeding helps prevent Wernicke\'s encephalopathy caused by thiamine deficiency.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3368, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-108', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A unilateral hypoglossal nerve lesion characteristically causes', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A lower motor neuron lesion of the hypoglossal nerve causes the tongue to deviate toward the affected side when protruded.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3369, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-109', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The gold standard for definitive cancer diagnosis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Definitive cancer diagnosis requires tissue examination by biopsy and histopathology.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3370, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-110', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Long-term lithium therapy most commonly causes', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Long-term lithium therapy can impair thyroid function and commonly causes hypothyroidism.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3371, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-111', 'mcq', 'hard', 'A common early side effect of a subdermal contraceptive implant is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Irregular or unpredictable vaginal bleeding is a common early effect of contraceptive implants.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3372, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-112', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which state does hepatic gluconeogenesis primarily occur during?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hepatic gluconeogenesis becomes particularly important during prolonged fasting to maintain blood glucose levels.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3373, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-113', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The antihypertensive action of thiazide diuretics in long-term use is BEST explained by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Although thiazides initially reduce plasma volume, their long-term antihypertensive effect is mainly related to decreased peripheral vascular resistance.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3374, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-114', 'mcq', 'hard', 'The most reliable indicator of adequate fluid resuscitation in the first 24 hours after a major burn is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Urine output is a practical indicator of renal perfusion and adequacy of fluid resuscitation in major burns.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3375, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-115', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In event where it is difficult to reach a group/set of population for the study in terms of locating them (eg Albinos), the researcher may apply??? sampling technique', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Snowball sampling is useful for reaching hard-to-locate or relatively hidden populations through referrals from existing participants.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3376, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-116', 'mcq', 'hard', 'In nursing care plan evaluation should be in line with', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Evaluation determines whether the stated nursing objectives or expected outcomes have been achieved.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
(3377, 9, 30, NULL, 'AD-DEV-117', 'mcq', 'hard', 'Which set does pterion skull landmark represent junction of?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The pterion is the junction of the frontal, parietal, temporal and greater wing of sphenoid bones.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-10 15:07:45', '2026-10-10 15:07:45', NULL),
