(5292, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-50', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client is experiencing bladder spasms after catheterization. The nurse should first', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Bladder spasms may result from catheter obstruction or malposition. Checking catheter patency and drainage is the initial step.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5293, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-51', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A neutropenic patient\'s room is being prepared by the nurse. Which item should be removed from a neutropenic patient\'s room?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Fresh flowers and plants may harbor bacteria and fungi that can expose immunocompromised patients to infection.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5294, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-52', 'mcq', 'medium', 'One of these is NOT a pressure group in Nigeria', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The Nursing and Midwifery Council of Nigeria is a regulatory body, whereas the other organizations are labour or staff unions that advocate for members\' interests.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5295, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-53', 'mcq', 'medium', 'How do the kidneys respond to low plasma sodium and low blood pressure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Reduced renal perfusion and reduced sodium chloride delivery to the macula densa stimulate renin release by juxtaglomerular cells.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5296, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-54', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient does exactly the opposite of what is asked. This behaviour is termed', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Negativism is resistance to instructions or doing the opposite of what is requested, and may occur in catatonia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5297, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-55', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A major complication of any hormonal method requiring urgent action is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A severe headache may indicate a serious complication, such as markedly elevated blood pressure or a cerebrovascular event, and requires urgent assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5298, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-56', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 2-month-old infant has projectile vomiting after feeds and remains hungry. The most likely diagnosis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pyloric stenosis classically presents in early infancy with projectile, usually non-bilious vomiting and continued hunger after vomiting.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5299, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-57', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which artery supplies medial breast tissue?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Perforating branches of the internal thoracic artery supply much of the medial breast tissue.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5300, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-58', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Myocardial infarction is primarily characterised by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Myocardial infarction involves irreversible death of myocardial cells due to prolonged ischaemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5301, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-59', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Cortisol is produced by which gland?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cortisol is produced by the adrenal cortex and helps regulate the stress response, metabolism and inflammation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5302, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-60', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which component do peripheral chemoreceptors primarily detect decreases in?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Peripheral chemoreceptors, particularly the carotid bodies, respond strongly to reduced arterial oxygen partial pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5303, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-61', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Diabetes that develops during pregnancy and usually resolves after delivery is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Gestational diabetes is glucose intolerance first recognized during pregnancy and often resolves after delivery, although follow-up screening is important.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5304, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-62', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Herd immunity protects susceptible people mainly by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'When a sufficient proportion of a population is immune, transmission decreases and susceptible people are less likely to encounter the pathogen.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5305, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-63', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A pregnant woman on a strict vegan diet may need supplementation of which vitamin?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vitamin B12 is found naturally mainly in animal-derived foods, so people following a strict vegan diet generally need a reliable fortified source or supplementation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5306, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-64', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client with heart failure is advised to call their doctor if they experience a weight gain of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rapid weight gain may indicate fluid retention and worsening heart failure. The client should follow their individualized reporting threshold and care plan.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5307, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-65', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In abdominal injury, pain in the left upper quadrant may be a clinical manifestation of injury to the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The spleen lies in the left upper quadrant, and injury may cause pain in that region.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5308, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-66', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse entrepreneur offers free blood pressure checks at a market to attract clients. This marketing strategy is best described as', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Providing free screening in a public setting raises awareness, builds trust and introduces services to the community.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5309, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-67', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The priority in caring for a child on long-term corticosteroid therapy is to prevent', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Long-term corticosteroid therapy suppresses immune responses and increases susceptibility to infection.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5310, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-68', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Exogenous antigens are presented to CD4 T-helper cells on', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Antigen-presenting cells process exogenous antigens and present them on MHC class II molecules to CD4 T-helper cells.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5311, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-69', 'mcq', 'medium', 'During nursing care-plan evaluation, which earlier planning element supplies the standard against which progress is judged?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Previously stated expected outcomes provide measurable criteria for evaluating whether nursing goals have been achieved.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5312, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-70', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client is prescribed a statin medication like atorvastatin. The nurse must instruct the client to report which symptom immediately?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Unexplained muscle pain or weakness may indicate statin-associated muscle injury. Severe symptoms or dark urine require urgent medical assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5313, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-71', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A possible complication after insertion of a contraceptive implant is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Local infection can occur at the insertion site because the procedure breaks the skin.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5314, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-72', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Caput succedaneum is often associated with moulding but is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Caput succedaneum is scalp oedema that crosses suture lines because it involves superficial tissues.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5315, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-73', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient on a depot antipsychotic develops mild injection site reactions. The most appropriate first step is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Reviewing the injection technique, site selection and administration procedure may identify a correctable cause of mild local reactions.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5316, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-74', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The process by which a drug moves from its site of administration into the bloodstream is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Absorption is the movement of a drug from its administration site into the systemic circulation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5317, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-75', 'mcq', 'medium', 'When ethical principles conflict, the MOST IMPORTANT initial nursing action is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Recognizing and clearly identifying the ethical conflict is the first step toward appropriate ethical decision-making.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5318, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-76', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client with osteoarthritis is considering a total knee replacement. The primary indication for this surgery is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Total knee replacement is considered when severe persistent pain and loss of function continue despite appropriate non-surgical treatment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5319, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-77', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which hypothalamic hormone controls water balance?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Antidiuretic hormone (ADH) is produced in the hypothalamus and released by the posterior pituitary. It helps regulate water balance by reducing urine production.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5320, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-78', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with myxedema coma requires emergency treatment. IV levothyroxine is given to replace which hormone?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Levothyroxine is a synthetic form of thyroid hormone used to treat severe hypothyroidism, including myxedema coma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5321, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-79', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The part of the inner ear that is involved in hearing is called the:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The cochlea converts sound vibrations into electrical nerve signals for hearing.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5322, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-80', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Motor nerves conduct impulses from the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Motor nerves carry impulses from the central nervous system to muscles, enabling movement.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5323, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-81', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Mrs. Halima, 62-year-old hypertensive with history of gout, which drug should be avoided?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Hydrochlorothiazide can increase uric acid levels and worsen gout.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5324, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-82', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The main reason for giving IPTp-SP as directly observed therapy is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Directly observed therapy confirms that the patient swallows the prescribed dose of intermittent preventive treatment for malaria in pregnancy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5325, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-83', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Right-sided body weakness after stroke indicates a lesion in the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The left cerebral hemisphere controls most voluntary movement on the right side of the body.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5326, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-84', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is caring for a patient with a diagnosis of cirrhosis. Which of the following findings is most concerning?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Decreased consciousness may indicate hepatic encephalopathy, a serious complication requiring immediate assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5327, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-85', 'mcq', 'medium', 'An arterial pulse with a brisk rise followed by rapid collapse is a', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A water-hammer pulse has a rapid, forceful rise followed by a sudden collapse.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5328, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-86', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with cancer receives intranasal fentanyl. This rapid-onset formulation is designed for', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Rapid-onset fentanyl formulations are designed to treat sudden episodes of breakthrough cancer pain in appropriately selected opioid-tolerant patients.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5329, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-87', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Administering pethidine to a woman in advanced labour (8 cm dilated) carries a significant risk of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pethidine crosses the placenta, and administration close to delivery may depress the newborn\'s respiratory effort.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5330, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-88', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which enzyme in tears has an antibacterial action?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Lysozyme helps protect the eyes by breaking down components of bacterial cell walls.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5331, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-89', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which vitamin deficiency causes pellagra?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pellagra results from niacin deficiency and classically causes dermatitis, diarrhoea and dementia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5332, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-90', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A receptor superfamily that binds lipophilic ligands, migrates to DNA, and modulates transcriptional activity is termed:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Nuclear receptors bind lipid-soluble ligands and regulate gene transcription through interactions with DNA.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5333, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-91', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient is prescribed tenofovir-based regimen. TDF requires monitoring of which organ function?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) can affect kidney function, so renal function should be monitored during treatment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5334, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-92', 'mcq', 'medium', 'When educating a community about building a simple pit latrine, the nurse should stress which feature?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A cover helps prevent flies and pests from entering, reduces odour and lowers the risk of accidental falls.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5335, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-93', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The vestibular apparatus consists of all of the following structures EXCEPT the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The utricle, saccule and semicircular ducts are involved in balance. The cochlear duct is primarily concerned with hearing.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:16', '2026-10-13 15:58:16', NULL),
(5336, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-94', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with hyperthyroidism has exophthalmos, heat intolerance and weight loss. The first-line antithyroid drug is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Carbimazole inhibits thyroid hormone synthesis and is commonly used as first-line treatment for hyperthyroidism. Propranolol may be added for symptom control.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5337, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-95', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient on antihypertensive asks about salt restriction. Dietary sodium reduction to less than 2300 mg/day helps lower BP by which mechanism?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Reducing sodium intake decreases fluid retention and can lower blood volume and blood pressure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5338, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-96', 'mcq', 'medium', 'After a needle-stick exposure to HIV-positive blood, the latest time by which post-exposure prophylaxis should be started is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'HIV post-exposure prophylaxis should begin as soon as possible, ideally within 24 hours and no later than 72 hours after exposure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5339, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-97', 'mcq', 'medium', 'An older adult is at higher risk of dehydration than a younger adult mainly because of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Older adults may have a reduced thirst response and reduced ability to conserve water, increasing their risk of dehydration.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5340, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-98', 'mcq', 'medium', 'On abdominal palpation soon after placental expulsion, the fundus of the uterus should be located', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Following placental expulsion, the contracted uterine fundus is typically central and around the level of the umbilicus or slightly below it.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5341, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-99', 'mcq', 'medium', 'All of the following are recognised methods of correcting acute uterine inversion EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Symphysiotomy widens the pelvis and is not a method of correcting uterine inversion. Manual replacement and selected hydrostatic or surgical techniques may be used.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5342, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-100', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A pregnant woman with recurrent pregnancy loss reports cramping and vaginal spotting. The midwife should', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vaginal bleeding and cramping during pregnancy require prompt assessment for threatened miscarriage and other possible complications.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5343, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-101', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Pressure ulcers most commonly develop over', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Prolonged pressure over bony prominences can compress blood vessels, reduce tissue perfusion and cause pressure injuries.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5344, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-102', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The community health nurse discusses cancer prevention strategies. Which of the following behaviors is NOT a cancer prevention measure?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Processed meat consumption is associated with increased risk of certain cancers, particularly colorectal cancer, and is not a preventive measure.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(5345, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-103', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A pregnant patient with DVT history needs thromboprophylaxis. Low Molecular Weight Heparin is preferred because it has which advantage?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Low molecular weight heparin has predictable anticoagulant effects and usually requires less routine laboratory monitoring than unfractionated heparin. It does not cross the placenta.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5346, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-104', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The functional part of the kidney tissue is known as the:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The renal parenchyma is the functional tissue of the kidney and consists of the cortex and medulla.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5347, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-105', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Spinal accessory nerve damage primarily weakens which muscle group function set?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The spinal accessory nerve (cranial nerve XI) supplies the sternocleidomastoid and trapezius muscles, which support head turning and shoulder elevation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5348, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-106', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Dan-lami lives in the squatter area. He goes to a nearby school and helps his mother gather oranges after school. One day, he is absent because of fever, malaise, anorexia and abdominal discomfort. Which of the following is concurrent disinfection in his case?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Concurrent disinfection involves the proper disposal or disinfection of infectious materials during the period of illness to prevent the spread of pathogens.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5349, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-107', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In the OPQRST mnemonic for symptom assessment, the letter Q stands for', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Q stands for quality and describes the character or nature of a symptom.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5350, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-108', 'mcq', 'medium', 'According to Freud, neurotic anxiety arises from', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Neurotic anxiety arises from unconscious conflict involving the id and ego, particularly the fear that unacceptable impulses may overwhelm the ego.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5351, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-109', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A small blood spill is noticed beside a patient\'s bed while visitors are nearby. What should the nurse do first?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Restricting access prevents accidental contact with the blood spill before the nurse cleans it using appropriate personal protective equipment and disinfectant.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5352, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-110', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client is prescribed methimazole for hyperthyroidism. The nurse understands that this medication', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Methimazole inhibits thyroid hormone synthesis by blocking thyroid peroxidase activity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5353, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-111', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The most common cause of acute upper gastrointestinal bleeding in cirrhotic patients is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Portal hypertension associated with cirrhosis can cause oesophageal varices, which may rupture and produce severe upper gastrointestinal bleeding.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5354, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-112', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The initial fluid of choice for resuscitating a patient with sepsis-induced hypoperfusion is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Isotonic crystalloids, including balanced crystalloid solutions, are recommended as first-line fluids for initial resuscitation in sepsis-induced hypoperfusion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5355, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-113', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The best first aid for a simple nosebleed in a child is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Leaning forward and pinching the soft part of the nose continuously helps control bleeding and prevents blood from being swallowed.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5356, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-114', 'mcq', 'medium', 'After heavy bleeding, a patient is restless with a weak, rapid pulse. Which finding best supports early hypoperfusion?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cool, clammy skin may indicate peripheral vasoconstriction caused by reduced circulating blood volume and poor tissue perfusion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5357, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-115', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The following are types of budget EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Simple budget is not a commonly recognized formal budget classification, whereas zero-based and fixed budgets are established budget types.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5358, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-116', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Home blood pressure monitoring is especially useful for identifying', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'White-coat hypertension occurs when blood pressure is elevated in a clinical setting but is normal outside the clinic, as demonstrated by home or ambulatory readings.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5359, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-117', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The following are risk factors for developing puerperal postnatal depression EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Spontaneous vaginal delivery is not generally considered a specific risk factor for postnatal depression, unlike factors such as a history of mental health problems or traumatic birth experiences.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5360, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-118', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A school-aged patient with attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder is displaying disruptive behaviours at home. The psychiatric and mental health nurse modifies the treatment plan for the social domain by advising the patient\'s parents to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A point system uses positive reinforcement to encourage appropriate social behaviours and help the child develop better behavioural patterns.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5361, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-119', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Paediatric chronic pain programmes primarily emphasise', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Paediatric chronic pain programmes aim to improve daily functioning, physical activity, school attendance and quality of life rather than focusing only on pain elimination.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5362, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-120', 'mcq', 'medium', 'All of the following are characteristic of glaucoma EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Glaucoma typically causes progressive optic nerve damage and peripheral visual field loss. Sudden painless central vision loss is not the typical presentation of chronic glaucoma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5363, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-121', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The ability to delay gratification indicates maturation of the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The ego helps regulate impulses by balancing instinctive desires with reality, allowing a person to delay gratification.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5364, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-122', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A vial contains 40 mg/mL, and the prescribed dose is 26 mg. Calculate the volume to draw.', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Volume = prescribed dose ? concentration = 26 mg ? 40 mg/mL = 0.65 mL.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5365, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-123', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which type of epithelium is found in thyroid follicles?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Thyroid follicles are normally lined by simple cuboidal epithelial cells, although their height may vary with gland activity.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5366, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-124', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In the cardiac cycle, what is the phase called when the ventricles are filling with blood?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Diastole is the relaxation phase of the cardiac cycle during which the ventricles fill with blood.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5367, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-125', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is a primary area of specialisation in medical sociology?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Medical sociology examines how social and cultural factors influence health, illness behaviour, healthcare access and care-seeking practices.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5368, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-126', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which equipment do droplet precautions primarily require?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A medical or surgical mask is generally used for routine droplet precautions, alongside standard precautions and other measures appropriate to the infection.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5369, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-127', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A breastfeeding mother has full, tender breasts, and the baby struggles to attach. What is the safest instruction?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Expressing a small amount of milk before feeding can soften the areola and help the baby attach more effectively. Frequent effective feeding also helps relieve engorgement.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5370, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-128', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which cranial nerve is responsible for vision?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The optic nerve carries visual information from the retina to the brain.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5371, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-129', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The epidemic curve of a point-source outbreak typically shows', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A point-source outbreak usually produces a single peak because affected individuals are exposed to the same source over a relatively short period.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5372, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-130', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which muscle set is primarily supplied by the trigeminal nerve motor root?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The motor root of the trigeminal nerve, mainly through its mandibular division, supplies the muscles of mastication and muscles such as the tensor tympani.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5373, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-131', 'mcq', 'medium', 'An example of a probability sampling technique includes', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Systematic sampling is a probability sampling technique in which participants are selected at regular intervals from an appropriately arranged sampling frame, usually with a random start.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5374, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-132', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nurse evaluates whether the care plan was effective during', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The evaluation phase determines whether the expected outcomes of nursing care have been achieved.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5375, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-133', 'mcq', 'medium', 'All of the following are caused by improper nutrient intake EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Malaria is a parasitic disease transmitted by infected female Anopheles mosquitoes, not a nutritional deficiency disease.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5376, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-134', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In the Szasz-Hollender model, the active-passive relationship applies when', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The active-passive relationship applies when a patient cannot participate in care, such as when unconscious, and the healthcare professional acts on the patient\'s behalf.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5377, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-135', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Following head injury, a patient passes large amounts of dilute urine and becomes very thirsty. The nurse should suspect reduced release of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Reduced antidiuretic hormone release can cause central diabetes insipidus, resulting in excessive dilute urine and increased thirst.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5378, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-136', 'mcq', 'medium', 'An abnormally increased white blood cell count is a characteristic of which disease?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Leukaemia is a cancer of blood-forming tissues that may cause abnormal production and accumulation of white blood cells.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5379, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-137', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Signs of magnesium sulfate toxicity are assessed by monitoring', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Loss of deep tendon reflexes and respiratory depression are important signs of magnesium sulfate toxicity. Urine output should also be monitored because impaired renal excretion increases toxicity risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5380, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-138', 'mcq', 'medium', 'According to Freud, objective anxiety arises from', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Objective anxiety is a response to a real external danger or threat.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
(5381, 9, 33, NULL, 'AF-DEV-139', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is considered a medical treatment for coronary artery disease?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Oral medications, such as antianginal drugs and antiplatelet agents, are used in the medical management of coronary artery disease.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-13 15:58:17', '2026-10-13 15:58:17', NULL),
