(5565, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 71', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In shoulder dystocia, the most appropriate initial manoeuvre is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The McRoberts manoeuvre is a first-line intervention; fundal pressure should be avoided because it can worsen the obstruction.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5566, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 72', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse observes a sudden rhythm change on a client\'s cardiac monitor: absent P waves, irregular wavy baseline, narrow QRS (0.08 sec), and rate of 120 bpm. Which rhythm does this represent', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Atrial fibrillation produces absent distinct P waves, an irregular baseline, and usually narrow QRS complexes unless conduction is abnormal.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5567, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 73', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In entrepreneurship, risk-taking means', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Risk-taking involves making informed decisions despite uncertainty about outcomes.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5568, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 74', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which area mediates micturition inhibition during social situations?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The prefrontal cortex helps voluntarily inhibit urination when it is socially inappropriate.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5569, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 75', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The incubation period is the:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The incubation period is the time between infection and the onset of symptoms.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5570, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 76', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The receptors whose stimulation gives rise to pain are known as:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Nociceptors detect potentially damaging stimuli and transmit pain signals.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5571, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 77', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which concept does Watson caring theory primarily center on?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Jean Watson\'s theory emphasizes human caring and the transpersonal nurse-patient relationship.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5572, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 78', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The Bamako Initiative mainly introduced', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The Bamako Initiative promoted community participation and cost sharing to support essential primary healthcare services.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5573, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 79', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A sudden drop in blood pressure after spinal anesthesia is primarily due to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Spinal anesthesia can block sympathetic nerves, causing vasodilation and reduced venous return.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5574, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 80', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with acute upper GI bleeding requires resuscitation. IV pantoprazole is given to reduce gastric acid by which mechanism?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pantoprazole inhibits the gastric H+/K+ ATPase proton pump, reducing acid secretion.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5575, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 81', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with celiac disease should avoid', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Celiac disease is an immune-mediated reaction to gluten found in wheat, barley, and rye.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5576, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 82', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A child has a wheeze that is heard on auscultation. The nurse knows this is a sign of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Wheezing is usually caused by narrowed lower airways, often due to bronchospasm or inflammation.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5577, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 83', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A 24-year-old client presents to the emergency department protesting \"I am God.\" The nurse identifies this as a:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A fixed false belief about one\'s identity or powers may be a delusion of grandeur.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5578, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 84', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The therapy that aims to change behavior by identifying and reinforcing desired behaviors is known as what.', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Behavior modification uses learning principles, including reinforcement, to increase or decrease specific behaviors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5579, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 85', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The most severe form of postpartum psychiatric illness, characterised by delusions, hallucinations and risk of harm to self or baby, is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Postpartum psychosis is a psychiatric emergency requiring urgent specialist assessment and protection of mother and baby.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5580, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 86', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which aspect does nursing diagnosis primarily differ from medical by?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Nursing diagnoses focus on human responses to health conditions and life processes rather than solely identifying diseases.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5581, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 87', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Nursing measure that can raise intracranial pressure and should be limited is:', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Deep suctioning and hip flexion can increase intracranial pressure and should be minimized when possible.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5582, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 88', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The theorist who described survival needs as the most basic human needs is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Maslow\'s hierarchy places physiological and survival needs at the foundational level.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5583, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 89', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following cranial nerves controls the hearing', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Cranial nerve VIII, the vestibulocochlear nerve, transmits hearing and balance information.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5584, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 90', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which statement compares scores between two groups rather than describing a correlation between two measured variables?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'This statement compares scores between two groups, women and men, rather than describing a relationship between two continuous variables.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5585, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 91', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A client\'s surgical wound has dehisced and eviscerated. The nurse\'s priority intervention is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sterile saline-moistened gauze protects exposed organs; do not attempt to reinsert them, and obtain urgent surgical assistance.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5586, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 92', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A pregnant patient requires antibiotic therapy for infection. Fluoroquinolones are avoided due to concerns about which fetal effect?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Fluoroquinolones are generally avoided during pregnancy when suitable alternatives exist because of concerns about developing cartilage and musculoskeletal tissues.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5587, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 93', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse tells a patient, \'I will hurt you if you refuse this injection.\' This act is an example of', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Assault involves a threat of imminent unwanted physical contact; battery involves the actual unlawful contact.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5588, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 94', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A woman presents with painless bright red vaginal bleeding at 37 weeks? gestation. What is the most likely diagnosis?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Placenta previa classically presents with painless bright red vaginal bleeding in late pregnancy.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5589, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 95', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The strongest physiological stimulus for ADH release is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Increased plasma osmolality stimulates ADH release to conserve water in the kidneys.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5590, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 96', 'mcq', 'medium', 'At what angle do you insert the needle to administer an intradermal injection?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Intradermal injections are administered at a shallow angle, usually about 5?15 degrees.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5591, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 97', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following women is at highest risk in pregnancy on the basis of age?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Adolescent pregnancy, particularly at younger ages, is associated with increased risks, although individual risk also depends on health and social factors.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5592, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 98', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Ten days postpartum, a mother reports voices commanding harm to her baby; the nurse should first', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Command hallucinations involving harm to a baby require immediate safety measures and urgent psychiatric assessment.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5593, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 99', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The neuron type that conducts impulses from the spinal cord to skeletal muscle is best classified as', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Motor neurons carry efferent impulses from the central nervous system to skeletal muscles.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5594, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 100', 'mcq', 'medium', 'All of the following are non-governmental organisations that contribute to health care EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The State Ministry of Health is a government institution, while the other options are non-governmental organisations.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5595, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 101', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The nursing management of deep vein thrombosis includes anticoagulation and', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Anticoagulation prevents clot extension and new clot formation. Mobilisation may be encouraged when the patient is appropriately treated and clinically stable; vigorous leg massage should be avoided.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5596, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 102', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Services that are attractive to young people and provide a comfortable setting for their needs are called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Youth-friendly services are designed to be accessible, acceptable and responsive to young people\'s health needs.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5597, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 103', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which of the following is a contraindication to aspirin therapy?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'An active peptic ulcer increases the risk of gastrointestinal irritation and bleeding with aspirin.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5598, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 104', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Progestogen is added to oestrogen HRT in women with an intact uterus mainly to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Progestogen protects the endometrium against excessive growth and hyperplasia caused by unopposed oestrogen.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5599, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 105', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The most basic units about which information is collected in research studies are called the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'An element is the basic unit about which information is collected in a research study.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5600, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 106', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A research study in which data are collected from participants at a single point in time is a', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A cross-sectional study collects information from participants at one point in time.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5601, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 107', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Where is a drug placed when given by the buccal route?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The buccal route involves placing medication between the cheek and gum for absorption through the oral mucosa.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5602, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 108', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The most abundant leukocyte in adult peripheral blood is the', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Neutrophils normally make up the largest proportion of circulating white blood cells in adults.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5603, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 109', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The primary purpose of a workplace risk assessment is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Risk assessment identifies workplace hazards and determines measures to eliminate or reduce associated risks.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5604, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 110', 'mcq', 'medium', 'When using Clark?s formula, adult dose is 300 mg and child?s weight is 21 kg. Child?s dose is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Clark\'s formula: child dose = weight in pounds ? 150 ? adult dose. A weight of 21 kg is approximately 46.3 lb; 46.3 ? 150 ? 300 mg ? 92.6 mg, closest to 90 mg.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5605, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 111', 'mcq', 'medium', 'There are how many bones in the human skeleton?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The typical adult human skeleton contains 206 bones.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5606, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 112', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The white, cheese-like substance covering the skin of a newborn is called', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Vernix caseosa is the white, creamy protective substance covering a newborn\'s skin.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5607, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 113', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The hypercoagulable state of pregnancy, a component of Virchow\'s triad, is due to an increase in', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Pregnancy increases several clotting factors and reduces fibrinolytic activity, making blood more prone to clotting.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5608, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 114', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The hormone that lowers blood glucose level is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Insulin lowers blood glucose by promoting glucose uptake by cells and storage as glycogen.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5609, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 115', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A key hygiene message for preventing trachoma is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Regular face washing helps reduce eye discharge and transmission of trachoma.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5610, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 116', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Ernest Shonekan\'s Interim National Government was overthrown in November 1993 by', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'General Sani Abacha seized power in November 1993, ending the Interim National Government.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5611, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 117', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A nurse is unsure about a prescribed dose. The most appropriate action is to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The nurse should clarify an uncertain prescription with the prescriber before administering the medication.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5612, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 118', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which laboratory value is most indicative of anemia?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Decreased hemoglobin is a key laboratory indicator of anemia.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5613, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 119', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A resilient entrepreneur is best described as one who', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Resilience involves adapting to challenges and continuing after setbacks.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5614, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 120', 'mcq', 'medium', 'For a dehydrated patient receiving oral rehydration, the most measurable goal by next shift is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Urine output is an observable measure of hydration, although the adequacy of output should also be assessed.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5615, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 121', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Female sexual arousal disorder may be caused by all of the following EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Regular physical exercise is not generally a cause of female sexual arousal disorder.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5616, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 122', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The healing of the placental site is a unique physiological process because it occurs through', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'The placental site heals through shedding of superficial tissue and regeneration of the endometrium.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5617, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 123', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A patient with contraction alkalosis requires volume expansion. Saline administration corrects alkalosis by expanding volume and providing which ion?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Chloride-containing saline helps the kidneys excrete bicarbonate and correct chloride-responsive contraction alkalosis.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5618, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 124', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Caesarean section carries a higher risk of puerperal sepsis than vaginal birth mainly because', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Caesarean section involves surgery and creates a wound that can become infected.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5619, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 125', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Loss of water through the skin and the respiratory tract is referred to as', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Insensible water loss occurs through evaporation from the skin and respiratory tract and is not easily measured directly.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5620, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 126', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Patient-controlled analgesia improves pain control by allowing the patient to', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Patient-controlled analgesia allows patients to administer prescribed doses using a device with safety limits.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5621, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 127', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Which antidepressant class selectively inhibits serotonin reuptake?', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors block serotonin reuptake into presynaptic neurons.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL);
INSERT INTO `cbt_questions` (`id`, `organization_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `question_code`, `question_type`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `question_image`, `question_image_alt`, `marks`, `negative_marks`, `explanation`, `hint`, `time_limit_seconds`, `is_randomizable`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(5622, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 128', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Airborne infection isolation rooms must be maintained at', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Negative pressure prevents contaminated air from escaping into adjacent areas.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5623, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 129', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Sterile gloves are required when the nurse', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sterile gloves are required for urinary catheter insertion to maintain aseptic technique.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5624, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 130', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A booking client with a history of irregular 40?45 day menstrual cycles reports her Last Menstrual Period (LMP) as 10th January. The most accurate method to determine her EDD is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'An early ultrasound is more reliable for dating pregnancy when menstrual cycles are irregular.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5625, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 131', 'mcq', 'medium', 'A woman ten days postpartum suddenly develops sharp chest pain, breathlessness and haemoptysis. The most likely diagnosis is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Sudden chest pain, breathlessness and haemoptysis in the postpartum period suggest pulmonary embolism, a medical emergency.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5626, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 132', 'mcq', 'medium', 'The warning sign of cancer represented by \"U\" in CAUTION is', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'U in the CAUTION warning mnemonic refers to an ulcer or sore that does not heal.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5627, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 133', 'mcq', 'medium', 'All of the following are examples of long term risk EXCEPT', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'A slippery fall is an immediate environmental hazard rather than a long-term disease risk.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5628, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 134', 'mcq', 'medium', 'Y-chromosome microdeletions (AZFa, AZFb, AZFc) cause', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Deletions in these Y-chromosome regions can impair sperm production and cause male infertility.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
(5629, 9, 38, NULL, 'AE.DAY 135', 'mcq', 'medium', 'In health promotion, advocacy for health mainly involves', NULL, NULL, 0.40, 0.00, 'Advocacy involves influencing decision-makers and policies to create conditions that support health.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'active', 7, NULL, '2026-10-15 10:30:53', '2026-10-15 10:30:53', NULL),
